1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,366
About a century ago, the late Great Sir,

2
00:00:03,433 --> 00:00:05,100
One hundred tomans in the money of that time,

3
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:06,500
Placed in a silver tray,

4
00:00:06,533 --> 00:00:09,133
And sent it as a gift to "Mozaffaroddin Mirza."

5
00:00:09,466 --> 00:00:10,133
In return,

6
00:00:10,633 --> 00:00:13,166
He received permission to seize a large garden,

7
00:00:13,633 --> 00:00:16,566
And built this mansion with other people's bricks and mortar.

8
00:00:17,366 --> 00:00:18,400
His son, Sir,

9
00:00:18,666 --> 00:00:19,633
The Patriarch,

10
00:00:19,666 --> 00:00:22,066
Who had carried the silver tray to the crown prince,

11
00:00:22,166 --> 00:00:23,833
Thinking that after his death,

12
00:00:23,866 --> 00:00:26,133
No discord or division would arise among his children,

13
00:00:26,466 --> 00:00:28,633
Built seven other mansions in the garden,

14
00:00:28,666 --> 00:00:30,466
And divided them among them.

15
00:00:31,166 --> 00:00:32,266
Dear Uncle Napoleon,

16
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:33,733
Who was the eldest son,

17
00:00:33,766 --> 00:00:34,966
After Sir’s death,

18
00:00:34,966 --> 00:00:36,800
Inherited both his mansion,

19
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:38,733
And his temperament,

20
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:40,866
And also the title of "Sir."

21
00:00:44,166 --> 00:00:44,966
Dear Uncle,

22
00:00:44,966 --> 00:00:48,866
Under the pretext of preserving the sacred family unity,

23
00:00:49,066 --> 00:00:51,400
Interfered so much in the lives of his brothers and sisters,

24
00:00:51,433 --> 00:00:52,166
That most of them,

25
00:00:52,466 --> 00:00:55,266
Either built walls around their houses,

26
00:00:55,833 --> 00:00:58,366
Or, through court orders, sold them and left.

27
00:00:59,233 --> 00:01:00,133
All that remained was

28
00:01:00,166 --> 00:01:03,200
Our house, which was my mother’s inheritance, not my father’s property,

29
00:01:03,866 --> 00:01:05,400
And Dear Uncle Colonel’s house,

30
00:01:05,666 --> 00:01:07,533
Who had managed to put up,

31
00:01:07,533 --> 00:01:09,500
A short iron fence around his courtyard.

32
00:01:10,733 --> 00:01:11,866
Dear Uncle Napoleon,

33
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:13,566
Like the spirit of Great Sir,

34
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:15,533
Lived in the lordly mansion,

35
00:01:15,533 --> 00:01:17,766
And from the large windows of this mansion,

36
00:01:17,933 --> 00:01:20,100
Which was in fact the ruling seat of the garden,

37
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:21,800
Kept an eye on everything.

38
00:01:23,433 --> 00:01:25,500
(Sound of a wall clock’s pendulum)

39
00:01:25,533 --> 00:01:26,233
Dear Uncle,

40
00:01:26,266 --> 00:01:30,133
Was fascinated by Napoleon Bonaparte, the Emperor of France!

41
00:01:30,533 --> 00:01:31,800
He saw many similarities,

42
00:01:31,833 --> 00:01:34,400
Between his own life and Napoleon’s life.

43
00:01:34,966 --> 00:01:37,466
Like Napoleon, he had seven brothers and sisters.

44
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:38,733
Like Napoleon,

45
00:01:38,766 --> 00:01:39,666
His childhood years,

46
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:42,066
Had passed in dreams of conquest.

47
00:01:42,300 --> 00:01:44,266
At the same age as young Napoleon,

48
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:45,766
He too had entered the military.

49
00:01:45,766 --> 00:01:46,266
And finally,

50
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:47,466
Just like Napoleon,

51
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:49,666
Thirteen years after marriage,

52
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:51,166
He had divorced his wife!

53
00:01:52,666 --> 00:01:55,466
The only thing his life lacked compared to Napoleon,

54
00:01:55,633 --> 00:01:58,833
Was the irreconcilable enmity of the English.

55
00:01:59,366 --> 00:02:00,433
But this gap, too,

56
00:02:00,466 --> 00:02:02,866
He filled with his powerful imagination!

57
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:06,300
A few simple missions around the towns of Kazerun and Mamasani

58
00:02:06,333 --> 00:02:07,066
That were related,

59
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:10,366
To his service in Colonel Liakhov’s Cossack regiment,

60
00:02:10,466 --> 00:02:12,333
Had turned, in his imagination,

61
00:02:12,566 --> 00:02:15,233
Into wars with cannons and rifles,

62
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:18,600
And with the military formations of Napoleon Bonaparte,

63
00:02:18,633 --> 00:02:20,033
At Austerlitz,

64
00:02:20,066 --> 00:02:21,500
And Waterloo.

65
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,366
(Sound of horses’ hooves)

