On the kids!

112
00:06:21,333 --> 00:06:22,400
Oh, my dear,

113
00:06:22,433 --> 00:06:24,700
Whatever he is, he’s the head of the family.

114
00:06:24,700 --> 00:06:26,200
He must be respected.

115
00:06:26,233 --> 00:06:28,100
I suppose those poor Cossacks too,

116
00:06:28,133 --> 00:06:30,100
Got a speech from him once a week at roll call!

117
00:06:30,533 --> 00:06:33,300
Napoleon was a saint compared to him.

118
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:42,700
Oh, good Lord!

119
00:06:46,033 --> 00:06:46,700
Siamak!

120
00:06:48,500 --> 00:06:49,933
Aren’t you coming to Dear Uncle’s house?!

121
00:06:49,933 --> 00:06:50,800
It’s still early!

122
00:06:50,833 --> 00:06:52,433
Why should I go stand there in the sun?!

123
00:06:53,066 --> 00:06:54,000
You don’t know why Dear Uncle,

124
00:06:54,033 --> 00:06:55,700
Has called the kids? - What do I know!

125
00:06:55,933 --> 00:06:58,800
Go ask Mash Ghasem!

126
00:06:58,833 --> 00:06:59,833
Alright.

127
00:07:13,066 --> 00:07:14,633
Oh, good Lord!

128
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:20,233
Damn every shameless Nastaran rose!

129
00:07:20,933 --> 00:07:21,800
Mash Ghasem!

130
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:26,500
Ouch! Our back is broken!

131
00:07:29,233 --> 00:07:31,400
Kid, you scared us!

132
00:07:31,466 --> 00:07:32,500
What’s my fault?!

133
00:07:32,566 --> 00:07:34,733
You fuss over this Nastaran yourself from morning to night!

134
00:07:34,766 --> 00:07:36,433
It’s Sir’s fault for loving this Nastaran,

135
00:07:36,466 --> 00:07:39,366
More than Miss Leili, his own daughter!

136
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:40,500
Ouch!

137
00:07:41,866 --> 00:07:43,000
Oh, good Lord!

138
00:07:43,033 --> 00:07:45,233
If Sir finds out we broke this branch,

139
00:07:45,233 --> 00:07:47,266
He’ll be the end of us!

140
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,400
Look what disaster has struck us!

141
00:07:50,433 --> 00:07:51,666
God willing, Sir won’t get wind of it.

142
00:07:51,700 --> 00:07:54,100
Did you have to call out to us, kid?!

143
00:07:54,500 --> 00:07:56,766
With all these branches and leaves, how would they know,

144
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:58,166
That you broke the Nastaran branch?

145
00:07:58,200 --> 00:08:00,366
Sir planted this Nastaran with his own hands.

146
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:02,266
You still don’t know Sir.

147
00:08:02,466 --> 00:08:04,000
Lord, let this end well.

148
00:08:08,433 --> 00:08:10,266
May God Himself have mercy on us.

149
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:11,800
In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.

150
00:08:12,066 --> 00:08:13,766
Have you gone mad, Mash Ghasem?!

151
00:08:13,833 --> 00:08:15,066
What do you want to do with it?

152
00:08:15,066 --> 00:08:16,466
Don’t let anything slip, kid,

153
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:17,966
In front of Sir!

154
00:08:18,433 --> 00:08:20,633
No, don’t worry… relax!

155
00:08:22,966 --> 00:08:23,666
Mash Ghasem!

156
00:08:23,666 --> 00:08:25,800
Don’t you know what’s happening here today?

157
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:27,433
Honestly, kid, why should I lie!

158
00:08:27,466 --> 00:08:29,800
The grave is this close!

159
00:08:29,966 --> 00:08:31,900
We don’t know, but Sir said,

160
00:08:31,933 --> 00:08:33,766
All the kids should gather today.

161
00:08:34,033 --> 00:08:36,400
You go quickly too… hurry… Sir will come out soon.

162
00:08:36,433 --> 00:08:36,900
Hurry!

163
00:08:36,900 --> 00:08:38,233
Go, kid… go!

164
00:08:56,633 --> 00:08:59,200
God rest its soul.

165
00:08:59,666 --> 00:09:01,133
Don’t you know what Dear Uncle wants with us? (The kids are whispering)

166
00:09:01,166 --> 00:09:03,300
I don’t know, it seems he wants to admonish me again.

167
00:09:03,433 --> 00:09:04,366
My place is here!

168
00:09:04,400 --> 00:09:06,033
- Go make yourself scarce, cheeky kid! - Get lost!

169
00:09:07,366 --> 00:09:09,466
Got a screw loose? - Shut up, fatso!

