00:09:09,533 --> 00:09:12,633
♪ National Anthem of France (La Marseillaise) ♪

171
00:09:29,066 --> 00:09:30,200
Hello, Dear Uncle!

172
00:09:30,233 --> 00:09:31,166
Dear Uncle, hello!

173
00:09:31,733 --> 00:09:32,700
Hello, Uncle!

174
00:09:32,766 --> 00:09:33,900
Hello, Dear Uncle!

175
00:09:34,900 --> 00:09:35,500
Hello, Uncle!

176
00:09:35,500 --> 00:09:37,500
Hello, Dear Uncle! Dear Uncle, hello!

177
00:09:37,900 --> 00:09:38,900
Hello, Sir!

178
00:09:38,933 --> 00:09:40,300
Hello, Dear Uncle!

179
00:09:40,400 --> 00:09:42,433
♪ Sound of military march ♪

180
00:09:57,033 --> 00:09:59,100
I was sixteen years old,

181
00:09:59,533 --> 00:10:01,400
But I had neither fallen in love,

182
00:10:01,633 --> 00:10:03,433
Nor seen a single person in love!

183
00:10:03,466 --> 00:10:04,933
H-h-h-hello…

184
00:10:04,966 --> 00:10:06,800
Remembering the fate of the lovers,

185
00:10:06,833 --> 00:10:09,266
I had read about in books terrified me.

186
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:12,233
All of them had a tragic fate,

187
00:10:12,433 --> 00:10:14,566
And their love always ended in death.

188
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:18,366
I was afraid that I, too, for the sin of loving Leili,

189
00:10:18,366 --> 00:10:19,933
Would be killed by Dear Uncle’s hands.

190
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:20,700
Ali!

191
00:10:20,733 --> 00:10:23,100
Why has Dear Uncle called the kids? - Honestly, I don’t know!

192
00:10:47,133 --> 00:10:49,266
♪ Music ♪

193
00:11:26,200 --> 00:11:29,200
Who blackened this wall with charcoal? (Writing on the wall: Napoleon is a donkey)

194
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:45,400
I said, who dirtied this wall with charcoal?

195
00:11:47,100 --> 00:11:49,033
(Sound of children’s laughter)

196
00:11:54,133 --> 00:11:55,766
- Oh… oh!

197
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:58,233
- Ouch! See, it’s Siamak’s doing!

198
00:11:58,233 --> 00:12:00,400
Get your hands off me, you bastard!

199
00:12:00,433 --> 00:12:01,700
I swear it wasn’t me, Dear Uncle!

200
00:12:01,733 --> 00:12:02,533
Ghasem, grab him!

201
00:12:02,533 --> 00:12:04,100
No, I swear it wasn’t me, Dear Uncle! (He’s crying)

202
00:12:04,100 --> 00:12:05,300
Don’t be scared, kid! - Let me go!

203
00:12:05,300 --> 00:12:07,300
Don’t make Sir so angry! - I swear it wasn’t me, Dear Uncle!

204
00:12:07,333 --> 00:12:09,000
Don’t let him escape, Ghasem!

205
00:12:09,300 --> 00:12:10,400
It’s all your fault!

206
00:12:10,766 --> 00:12:12,100
You were the one who told Dear Uncle,

207
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:13,533
That I write things on the wall!

208
00:12:13,566 --> 00:12:14,366
We didn’t tell, kid!

209
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:14,933
Then I’ll say,

210
00:12:14,966 --> 00:12:17,533
That you broke Dear Uncle’s Nastaran branch!

211
00:12:17,566 --> 00:12:18,400
Let him go!

212
00:12:18,433 --> 00:12:19,700
You broke it yourself!

213
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:23,133
Who broke the Nastaran branch?

214
00:12:23,433 --> 00:12:26,566
Who broke the Nastaran branch?! - I swear I’m not lying, Dear Uncle!

215
00:12:26,766 --> 00:12:28,066
Come, I’ll show you, Dear Uncle! - Who broke it!

216
00:12:28,100 --> 00:12:29,533
(Sound of commotion)

217
00:12:29,566 --> 00:12:30,633
I saw it myself, Dear Uncle!

218
00:12:30,666 --> 00:12:33,066
I swear by Saint Abbas, I saw it from behind the trees!

219
00:12:33,100 --> 00:12:35,000
He hid it here, Dear Uncle!

220
00:12:51,900 --> 00:12:52,900
Ghasem!

221
00:12:54,866 --> 00:12:56,133
Sir, forgive us!

222
00:12:56,566 --> 00:12:58,500
For God’s sake, forgive us, Sir!

223
00:12:58,533 --> 00:13:00,133
Forgive us, we did wrong, Sir!

224
00:13:00,166 --> 00:13:02,400
Shameless ingrate! (Sound of children’s commotion)

225
00:13:02,433 --> 00:13:04,100
Ignorant! - Oh, good Lord!

226
00:13:04,133 --> 00:13:04,966
Fool!

227
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:06,933
Traitor! - Forgive us, Sir, we did wrong

228
00:13:06,966 --> 00:13:07,633
Mercenary!

229
00:13:07,666 --> 00:13:08,800
Madman!

230
00:13:08,833 --> 00:13:10,100
Idiot!

231
00:13:10,133 --> 00:13:11,500
Impudent!

232
00:13:11,533 --> 00:13:13,533
Ignorant… scoundrel!

233
00:13:13,533 --> 00:13:14,533
Traitor!

234
00:13:14,566 --> 00:13:17,933
(Sound of children’s commotion)

235
00:13:19,133 --> 00:13:20,233
- Mash Ghasem, escape!

236
00:13:20,700 --> 00:13:21,466
What’s going on! - What’s going on, Sir?!

237
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:22,833
Kids, step aside!

238
00:13:22,866 --> 00:13:24,633
Stop him, he’ll kill him now! (Sound of commotion and Mash Ghasem’s groans)

239
00:13:24,666 --> 00:13:25,533
- Oh, good Lord!

240
00:13:25,566 --> 00:13:26,366
What has he done that he’ll kill him?!

241
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:27,866
Sir, remember all those wars,

242
00:13:27,900 --> 00:13:29,466
Where you saved our life?

243
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:30,800
Spiteful… good-for-nothing! (Commotion, groans, and pleas from Mash Ghasem)

244
00:13:30,833 --> 00:13:32,666
Saeed, what is it? What’s happened?

245
00:13:33,366 --> 00:13:36,200
You claim you were part of my army?

246
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:37,966
He broke the Nastaran branch!

247
00:13:38,666 --> 00:13:40,000
Babajoon is very angry!

248
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:40,600
I’m afraid he’ll kill Mash Ghasem!

249
00:13:40,633 --> 00:13:41,133
Don’t be afraid, Leili!

250
00:13:41,133 --> 00:13:44,033
What’s the matter? What’s happened? (Commotion, groans, and pleas from Mash Ghasem)

251
00:13:44,033 --> 00:13:45,100
Saeed!

252
00:13:45,133 --> 00:13:45,966
What’s going on?

253
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,333
Mash Ghasem broke the Nastaran branch!

254
00:13:48,333 --> 00:13:48,833
That’s it?!

255
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,666
Sir, I’m begging you!

256
00:13:52,333 --> 00:13:53,066
Why are you crying?

257
00:13:53,066 --> 00:13:54,500
Oh my God!

258
00:13:54,533 --> 00:13:55,866
Mama, he hit me!

259
00:13:55,900 --> 00:13:56,466
Who?!

260
00:13:57,400 --> 00:13:58,166
Dear Uncle!

261
00:13:58,200 --> 00:14:00,066
God damn him! Which Dear Uncle?

262
00:14:00,133 --> 00:14:01,400
Dear Uncle Napoleon!

263
00:14:01,433 --> 00:14:02,466
Bite your tongue, child!

264
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:03,500
Serves you right!

265
00:14:04,366 --> 00:14:05,133
Shut up, damn you!

266
00:14:05,133 --> 00:14:06,666
You wretch!

267
00:14:06,666 --> 00:14:08,133
Oh, good Lord!

268
00:14:08,133 --> 00:14:09,633
To think of all the sacrifices,

269
00:14:09,666 --> 00:14:11,266
That I made for you!

270
00:14:11,433 --> 00:14:13,233
There’s no place for you in this house anymore!

271
00:14:13,400 --> 00:14:14,133
Get lost!

272
00:14:14,166 --> 00:14:15,566
Sir, you’ll either have to get the police,

273
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:16,933
To throw us out of this house,

274
00:14:16,966 --> 00:14:18,300
Or carry out our corpse!

275
00:14:18,333 --> 00:14:20,533
We won’t leave on our own feet!

276
00:14:20,533 --> 00:14:21,066
Brother!

277
00:14:21,100 --> 00:14:23,000
Forgive him just this once!

278
00:14:23,033 --> 00:14:23,966
He did wrong!

279
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:24,700
He didn’t know better!

280
00:14:24,733 --> 00:14:27,300
Sir, you saved our life a hundred times!

281
00:14:27,433 --> 00:14:29,233
Now you want to take our life?!

282
00:14:29,333 --> 00:14:30,700
(He’s crying)

283
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:33,200
As long as we have life,

284
00:14:33,200 --> 00:14:35,333
We must serve you in this house.

285
00:14:35,633 --> 00:14:38,233
Who else would have done for us what you did?!

286
00:14:39,500 --> 00:14:42,066
Once in the Kazerun war, we were shot,

287
00:14:42,100 --> 00:14:43,900
Lying between two rocks…

288
00:14:43,933 --> 00:14:45,533
(Makes shooting sounds with his mouth)

289
00:14:45,866 --> 00:14:48,533
Bullets were pouring down like rain!

290
00:14:48,666 --> 00:14:51,433
We had already said our last prayers

291
00:14:51,666 --> 00:14:53,966
Vultures were circling,

292
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:56,133
In the sky above our heads,

293
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:57,266
Waiting for when we would die!

294
00:14:58,266 --> 00:15:00,100
Suddenly, bless him, Sir,

295
00:15:00,633 --> 00:15:02,933
God keep him great and noble,

296
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:04,533
May God grant him honor,

297
00:15:04,566 --> 00:15:05,933
In the midst of that hail of bullets,

298
00:15:05,933 --> 00:15:07,366
He reached us!

299
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:09,933
Like a lion, he threw us on his back!

300
00:15:10,433 --> 00:15:12,666
Carried us for miles,

301
00:15:12,700 --> 00:15:14,566
Until he brought us to our own trench!

302
00:15:15,066 --> 00:15:17,766
You think we could ever forget such things?

303
00:15:17,800 --> 00:15:18,933
If Sir wasn’t there,

304
00:15:18,933 --> 00:15:20,766
We’d be like poor Sultan Ali Khan,

305
00:15:20,800 --> 00:15:23,233
Long dead and buried by now!

306
00:15:29,500 --> 00:15:30,566
Poor thing!

307
00:15:31,700 --> 00:15:33,700
Poor Sultan Ali Khan!

308
00:15:35,566 --> 00:15:38,700
Ghasem, we wanted to do something for him too,

309
00:15:39,366 --> 00:15:41,400
But it wasn’t meant to be!

310
00:15:41,800 --> 00:15:43,533
May God have mercy on him.

311
00:15:43,566 --> 00:15:45,566
Brother!

312
00:15:45,566 --> 00:15:47,633
May I ask you a favor?

313
00:15:47,666 --> 00:15:49,533
Tomorrow night, would you kindly come

314
00:15:49,633 --> 00:15:51,033
And honor us.

315
00:15:51,133 --> 00:15:52,133
Tomorrow night?

316
00:15:52,166 --> 00:15:52,966
Yes, Dear Uncle!

317
00:15:53,100 --> 00:15:54,400
We want to be together.

318
00:15:55,100 --> 00:15:57,900
You see, Pouri Joon got his bachelor’s degree!

319
00:15:58,933 --> 00:16:01,566
Well done, boy! Well done!

320
00:16:01,900 --> 00:16:03,700
We will definitely come.

321
00:16:08,633 --> 00:16:09,266
Ghasem!

322
00:16:09,300 --> 00:16:09,800
Yes, Sir!

323
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:12,766
The kids dirtied this wall.

324
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:14,000
Clean it up quickly.

325
00:16:14,166 --> 00:16:15,000
Yes, Sir!

326
00:16:26,133 --> 00:16:27,600
That was a close call, Mash Ghasem!

327
00:16:27,700 --> 00:16:29,466
God bless Sir.

328
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,466
You must come too.

329
00:16:33,666 --> 00:16:34,633
It’ll be a good night.

330
00:16:34,633 --> 00:16:35,133
Alright!

331
00:16:36,166 --> 00:16:36,666
Let’s go.

332
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:38,366
Bless you, sister.

333
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:39,400
Bless you.

334
00:16:42,300 --> 00:16:42,800
Saeed!

335
00:16:43,033 --> 00:16:45,266
(Commotion of kids)

336
00:16:54,466 --> 00:16:55,166
Dear Leili!

337
00:16:55,400 --> 00:16:56,766
You must come too!

338
00:17:00,233 --> 00:17:03,233
After this incident, Dear Uncle officially accepted,

339
00:17:03,233 --> 00:17:06,300
That Mash Ghasem was with him in the wars!

340
00:17:07,300 --> 00:17:08,733
Thus, Mash Ghasem,

341
00:17:08,766 --> 00:17:10,700
Whose greatest feat in life,

342
00:17:11,033 --> 00:17:12,166
In the village of Ghias Abad,

343
00:17:12,166 --> 00:17:14,566
Was fighting with a few stray dogs,

344
00:17:15,100 --> 00:17:18,066
Joined the ranks of the brave warriors of the Kazerun war!

345
00:17:18,366 --> 00:17:20,433
♪ Chahargah Piece – Faramarz Payvar & Hossein Tehrani ♪

346
00:17:59,166 --> 00:17:59,766
Saeed!

347
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:01,100
What is it, Dear Shajoon?

348
00:18:02,600 --> 00:18:03,766
My darling!

349
00:18:03,766 --> 00:18:04,666
Your Agha Jan said tonight,

350
00:18:04,666 --> 00:18:06,066
We should send dinner for Mash Ghasem.

351
00:18:06,100 --> 00:18:06,766
For Mash Ghasem?!

352
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:08,233
Yes. The poor thing might be too shy

353
00:18:08,266 --> 00:18:09,600
To go to your Dear Uncle’s house tonight.

354
00:18:11,266 --> 00:18:12,000
Careful, dear.

355
00:18:14,533 --> 00:18:15,300
It’s hot, don’t burn yourself!

356
00:18:15,333 --> 00:18:16,000
No!

357
00:18:16,233 --> 00:18:18,366
♪ Traditional music ♪

358
00:18:32,866 --> 00:18:33,966
Oh, Imam Ali…

359
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:35,033
Mash Ghasem, how are you?

360
00:18:35,033 --> 00:18:36,166
Don’t ask, kid!

361
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:37,200
What’s this you brought?

362
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:38,333
I brought you dinner.

363
00:18:39,166 --> 00:18:40,166
It’s hot!

364
00:18:40,800 --> 00:18:42,333
My Dear Shajoon sent it for you!

365
00:18:42,766 --> 00:18:44,766
God bless her, kid,

366
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:46,100
For thinking of us!

367
00:18:46,900 --> 00:18:48,866
Are you preparing your lessons?

368
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:50,066
You’re doing well!

369
00:18:50,100 --> 00:18:53,000
There’s not much time left until the schools reopen!

370
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:54,366
It’s not lessons!

371
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:55,700
It’s a storybook!

372
00:18:55,900 --> 00:18:58,933
Instead of these books, you should learn to read the Quran,

373
00:18:58,966 --> 00:18:59,833
Kid!

374
00:19:05,866 --> 00:19:07,200
To be honest, Mash Ghasem…

375
00:19:07,633 --> 00:19:09,600
I came to ask you something.

376
00:19:10,366 --> 00:19:11,366
Go on, kid!

377
00:19:14,300 --> 00:19:15,700
I have a classmate,

378
00:19:15,733 --> 00:19:17,266
Who thinks he’s fallen in love!

379
00:19:17,633 --> 00:19:18,600
What?!

380
00:19:19,166 --> 00:19:20,300
I don’t know how to say it!

381
00:19:20,300 --> 00:19:21,500
He’s not sure!

382
00:19:21,533 --> 00:19:23,033
He’s too shy to ask anyone.

383
00:19:23,033 --> 00:19:24,600
He’s fallen in love?!

384
00:19:27,633 --> 00:19:29,200
You mean he’s become infatuated?!

385
00:19:29,233 --> 00:19:30,566
Your classmate?!

386
00:19:31,566 --> 00:19:32,166
Mash Ghasem!

387
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:33,866
Do you know how a person realizes,

388
00:19:33,866 --> 00:19:34,833
That they’ve fallen in love?

389
00:19:36,533 --> 00:19:38,166
Honestly, kid, why should I lie!

390
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:40,100
The grave is this close!

391
00:19:40,666 --> 00:19:42,500
We were smitten ourselves!

392
00:19:42,633 --> 00:19:44,033
No, no, no, no, we didn’t!

393
00:19:44,033 --> 00:19:44,600
We didn’t!

394
00:19:45,033 --> 00:19:46,233
I mean, yes we did!

395
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:47,866
Anyway, we know what a curse it is!

396
00:19:47,900 --> 00:19:49,100
No, no, no, kid! No!

397
00:19:50,100 --> 00:19:52,133
We were smitten ourselves,

398
00:19:52,166 --> 00:19:53,233
But you didn’t!

399
00:19:53,633 --> 00:19:56,166
Grown adults don’t survive it,

400
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:57,833
Let alone your classmate!

401
00:19:58,533 --> 00:19:59,766
But Mash Ghasem!

402
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:01,266
This classmate of mine,

403
00:20:01,300 --> 00:20:02,733
Who thinks he’s fallen in love,

404
00:20:03,433 --> 00:20:05,700
First wants to know if he’s really in love or not!

405
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,366
Then, if he sees he’s in love,

406
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:08,966
He wants to somehow cure his pain!

407
00:20:09,400 --> 00:20:11,100
Kid, you think love,

408
00:20:11,133 --> 00:20:12,133
Is that easy?!

409
00:20:12,133 --> 00:20:14,133
It’ll kill him, poor wretch!

410
00:20:20,400 --> 00:20:21,533
You still didn’t say how a person,

411
00:20:21,533 --> 00:20:23,033
Realizes they’ve fallen in love.

412
00:20:24,533 --> 00:20:26,333
Honestly, kid, why should I lie!

413
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:28,800
When you don’t see her,

414
00:20:29,133 --> 00:20:31,300
It’s like your heart turns to ice!

415
00:20:31,666 --> 00:20:33,066
When you see her,

416
00:20:33,500 --> 00:20:34,566
It’s like someone has lit

417
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:36,266
A baker’s oven in your heart!

418
00:20:36,833 --> 00:20:38,766
At least, that’s how it was for the one we knew!

419
00:20:39,133 --> 00:20:40,900
You want all the riches in the world

420
00:20:40,933 --> 00:20:41,866
For her!

421
00:20:42,100 --> 00:20:43,733
In short, you have no peace,

422
00:20:43,733 --> 00:20:45,966
Unless they get that girl engaged to you.

423
00:20:46,166 --> 00:20:48,000
But if she got married and left,

424
00:20:48,266 --> 00:20:51,200
Then God help you!!!

425
00:20:59,466 --> 00:21:02,333
There was someone in our town who became infatuated.

426
00:21:02,533 --> 00:21:04,933
♪ Segah – Gholamhossein Banan ♪

427
00:21:05,100 --> 00:21:06,266
One day, that girl,

428
00:21:06,266 --> 00:21:08,233
Was married off to someone else.

429
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:11,800
The next morning, our townsman,

430
00:21:11,833 --> 00:21:14,066
Headed off into the wilderness.

431
00:21:15,800 --> 00:21:17,633
Now twenty years have passed,

432
00:21:17,666 --> 00:21:20,033
And still, no one knows what happened!

433
00:21:21,300 --> 00:21:22,666
Where he went!

434
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:28,200
As if he went up in smoke,

435
00:21:29,233 --> 00:21:30,400
And vanished into the sky!

436
00:21:33,733 --> 00:21:36,533
(He sighs)

437
00:21:52,533 --> 00:21:54,166
(He gives a cold laugh)

438
00:22:07,033 --> 00:22:08,833
I should probably get going now.

439
00:22:12,800 --> 00:22:14,233
Are you coming tomorrow night?

440
00:22:14,366 --> 00:22:15,866
It’s the Colonel’s party.

441
00:22:16,066 --> 00:22:17,900
They’ve brought lots of tables and chairs.

442
00:22:18,133 --> 00:22:20,433
A party for Dear Pouri’s graduation!

443
00:22:21,500 --> 00:22:22,466
Oh, God…

444
00:22:22,566 --> 00:22:23,600
By the way, Mash Ghasem!

445
00:22:23,933 --> 00:22:25,100
Don’t let Dear Uncle find out,

446
00:22:25,133 --> 00:22:27,066
That I asked you about love and infatuation!

447
00:22:27,366 --> 00:22:28,666
Us? Tell Sir anything?!

448
00:22:29,466 --> 00:22:31,300
Are we tired of living?!

449
00:22:32,733 --> 00:22:35,533
If Sir hears talk of love and infatuation,

450
00:22:35,566 --> 00:22:37,000
He’ll raise hell!

451
00:22:37,300 --> 00:22:39,000
No offense, but he’d kill someone!

452
00:22:40,466 --> 00:22:43,000
God forbid someone falls in love with Miss Leili!

453
00:22:43,033 --> 00:22:45,700
I swear, Sir would wipe out his whole family!

454
00:22:45,833 --> 00:22:47,966
♪ Sound of military march ♪

455
00:23:03,300 --> 00:23:04,733
What happened, kid?!

456
00:23:08,800 --> 00:23:09,300
Nothing.

457
00:23:09,333 --> 00:23:10,500
I felt dizzy.

458
00:23:14,333 --> 00:23:15,433
Get up, come on… Ali!

459
00:23:32,133 --> 00:23:35,133
♪ Iranian music ♪

460
00:23:35,166 --> 00:23:38,333
Shahpour or Pouri, nicknamed the great genius,

461
00:23:38,400 --> 00:23:40,066
Son of Dear Uncle Colonel,

462
00:23:40,066 --> 00:23:42,700
Was the only one in our family to earn a bachelor’s degree.

463
00:23:43,066 --> 00:23:44,933
Dear Uncle Colonel was the kind of person,

464
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:47,600
Who loved to throw parties for any occasion.

465
00:23:48,233 --> 00:23:50,033
Dear Uncle Colonel wasn’t actually a colonel.

466
00:23:50,066 --> 00:23:52,900
He was a major, which back then they called "Yaavar."

467
00:23:52,933 --> 00:23:55,333
(Sound of group laughter)

468
00:23:55,900 --> 00:23:57,066
To your health! - To your health!

469
00:23:57,066 --> 00:23:59,300
To you, Pouri, and the lady!

470
00:23:59,333 --> 00:24:01,233
One night at a party,

471
00:24:01,266 --> 00:24:02,833
By the implicit decree of Dear Uncle Napoleon,

472
00:24:02,866 --> 00:24:05,033
Who had called him Brother Colonel,

473
00:24:05,066 --> 00:24:06,533
Gradually everyone got used to,

474
00:24:06,566 --> 00:24:08,666
Calling him Mr. Colonel.

475
00:24:09,600 --> 00:24:10,333
He and his wife,

476
00:24:10,366 --> 00:24:13,433
Had spoiled Pouri rotten.

477
00:24:13,933 --> 00:24:15,933
In my opinion, Pouri wasn’t a smart kid!

478
00:24:15,966 --> 00:24:19,100
He just studied like a workhorse!

479
00:24:19,133 --> 00:24:21,366
He memorized the lessons word for word,

480
00:24:21,400 --> 00:24:22,366
And got good grades.

481
00:24:23,666 --> 00:24:25,000
Until the age of eighteen,

482
00:24:25,100 --> 00:24:26,233
His mother held his hand,

483
00:24:26,266 --> 00:24:27,900
And walked him across the street!

484
00:24:29,233 --> 00:24:31,866
Hello, lady! Have you seen Aziz?

485
00:24:31,866 --> 00:24:33,000
You naughty thing!

486
00:24:33,100 --> 00:24:36,066
Don’t tell me you bumped her off?!

487
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:38,400
It’s a nice night… isn’t it?

488
00:24:38,433 --> 00:24:40,266
On nights like this, I’m in great spirits!

489
00:24:40,666 --> 00:24:42,100
You get to see the whole family.

490
00:24:42,100 --> 00:24:43,333
Especially me!

491
00:24:43,366 --> 00:24:44,500
Get lost, you clown!

492
00:24:44,500 --> 00:24:45,733
Mr. Dustali Khan,

493
00:24:45,766 --> 00:24:48,000
Was distantly related to our family,

494
00:24:48,033 --> 00:24:50,933
And was notorious among the women for his wandering eye.

495
00:24:51,433 --> 00:24:53,800
No one was better than Prince Asadollah Mirza,

496
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:56,033
Whose absence was felt at the party,

497
00:24:56,033 --> 00:24:57,533
At handling him.

498
00:24:57,800 --> 00:24:59,700
His wife, Mrs Aziz al-Saltaneh,

499
00:24:59,766 --> 00:25:01,400
Was a close relative of ours.

500
00:25:01,866 --> 00:25:03,066
Mrs Aziz al-Saltaneh,

501
00:25:03,100 --> 00:25:05,233
Had another husband before Dustali Khan,

502
00:25:05,466 --> 00:25:07,433
Who apparently had gone missing!

503
00:25:08,033 --> 00:25:10,333
Perhaps it was for Ghamar’s money

504
00:25:10,366 --> 00:25:11,633
That Mr. Dustali Khan

505
00:25:11,666 --> 00:25:13,833
Endured living with Mrs Aziz al-Saltaneh!

506
00:25:13,833 --> 00:25:14,766
He endured it!

507
00:25:15,266 --> 00:25:16,833
Dear Mrs Aziz, from her late husband,

508
00:25:16,833 --> 00:25:18,766
Had inherited a fat, dim-witted, greedy daughter,

509
00:25:18,800 --> 00:25:20,266
Named Ghamar,

510
00:25:20,500 --> 00:25:22,800
Who was not yet of age.

511
00:25:27,066 --> 00:25:28,466
Say, how about we tease,

512
00:25:28,500 --> 00:25:31,266
Dr. Naser Al-hokama a bit!

513
00:25:31,300 --> 00:25:32,666
Have some fun with him!

514
00:25:33,433 --> 00:25:34,033
There he is!

515
00:25:34,066 --> 00:25:35,366
That’s the guy! - Go!

516
00:25:35,533 --> 00:25:37,033
Prince Shamsali Mirza,

517
00:25:37,100 --> 00:25:39,300
The elder brother of Asadollah Mirza,

518
00:25:39,333 --> 00:25:40,966
Was an examining magistrate in the judiciary,

519
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:43,633
And had headed the Hamedan judiciary until two years ago,

520
00:25:43,666 --> 00:25:46,500
When, for some unknown reason, he was suspended.

521
00:25:47,100 --> 00:25:48,533
Due to his profession,

522
00:25:48,566 --> 00:25:50,466
He considered trial and interrogation,

523
00:25:50,500 --> 00:25:53,433
The key to solving all the world’s problems!

524
00:25:54,833 --> 00:25:56,233
Miss Farrokh Lagha,

525
00:25:56,266 --> 00:25:58,033
Was a jinxed old maid,

526
00:25:58,066 --> 00:25:59,033
Who once was supposed to,

527
00:25:59,066 --> 00:26:00,733
Become Mr. Dustali Khan’s wife.

528
00:26:00,766 --> 00:26:02,933
Poor thing, whenever she came through a door,

529
00:26:03,066 --> 00:26:05,400
Bad news followed her into that house!

530
00:26:05,400 --> 00:26:05,900
Sir!

531
00:26:06,433 --> 00:26:07,766
Sir has arrived!

532
00:26:12,933 --> 00:26:13,933
Hello, Brother!

533
00:26:13,933 --> 00:26:15,166
How kind of you to come! - Hello!

534
00:26:15,200 --> 00:26:16,066
You’ve done us a favor!

535
00:26:16,066 --> 00:26:17,166
Thank you!

536
00:26:17,166 --> 00:26:18,566
How are you, Dear Pouri?

537
00:26:18,600 --> 00:26:19,133
Hello!

538
00:26:19,166 --> 00:26:22,300
Hello. Congratulations, buddy… Well done! - Thanks!

539
00:26:22,600 --> 00:26:24,366
Wow! What a girl!

540
00:26:24,400 --> 00:26:25,900
Bless you, darling!

541
00:26:25,900 --> 00:26:27,300
What a pretty face!

542
00:26:27,300 --> 00:26:29,900
You’ll be a bride soon, kid! - Wow… wow… Naser Al-hokama!

543
00:26:29,933 --> 00:26:31,533
Let’s go see Brother. - She’s very lovely!

544
00:26:32,033 --> 00:26:34,033
- Oh! Shamsali Mirza is here too!

545
00:26:34,500 --> 00:26:35,166
Leili!

546
00:26:35,400 --> 00:26:36,100
Leili!

547
00:26:39,033 --> 00:26:39,933
Why are you standing here?

548
00:26:39,966 --> 00:26:43,533
I was waiting for you! Why were you late? - Well! Everybody’s here!

549
00:26:43,566 --> 00:26:44,833
(Commotion of guests)

550
00:26:44,933 --> 00:26:45,733
- Please, come in!

551
00:26:53,500 --> 00:26:57,900
I’m going to roll you a nice four and two!

552
00:26:57,933 --> 00:26:58,333
Look! Aha!

553
00:26:58,333 --> 00:26:58,900
Roll!

554
00:26:58,933 --> 00:26:59,633
Four and two!

555
00:26:59,666 --> 00:27:01,100
(Sound of laughter)

556
00:27:01,133 --> 00:27:03,066
Looks like you need to close your house!

557
00:27:03,100 --> 00:27:04,733
Yes… that’s the custom!

558
00:27:05,100 --> 00:27:08,200
Leave the battle to the real warriors!

559
00:27:08,233 --> 00:27:09,733
Roll the dice!

560
00:27:09,766 --> 00:27:10,866
Now watch

561
00:27:10,900 --> 00:27:12,766
How he holds the dice!

562
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:14,000
Roll! Come on, roll!

563
00:27:14,033 --> 00:27:14,866
You need to come to me,

564
00:27:14,900 --> 00:27:16,066
To learn how to roll dice!

565
00:27:16,100 --> 00:27:17,500
I need to teach you first,

566
00:27:17,533 --> 00:27:19,300
How to hold the dice in your hand!

567
00:27:19,333 --> 00:27:19,833
Look!

568
00:27:21,033 --> 00:27:21,800
Five and three.

569
00:27:21,833 --> 00:27:22,666
It was five and two!

570
00:27:22,700 --> 00:27:24,100
Come on… it was five and three! - It was five and two!

571
00:27:24,133 --> 00:27:25,233
Look for yourself, it was five and three! - It was five and two, five and two.

572
00:27:25,233 --> 00:27:26,333
It was five and two, Sir!

573
00:27:26,333 --> 00:27:27,833
No cheating, now! - Why did you pick them up?

574
00:27:27,933 --> 00:27:29,633
Why did you pick them up? It was five and two!

575
00:27:29,700 --> 00:27:30,700
Babajoon, what…

576
00:27:30,733 --> 00:27:32,000
What do you mean, it was five and two!

577
00:27:32,033 --> 00:27:33,066
It was five and three!

578
00:27:33,100 --> 00:27:36,366
It was five and two… five and two! (Commotion and argument)

579
00:27:36,400 --> 00:27:38,533
I swear to God it was five and three!

580
00:27:38,566 --> 00:27:40,300
I’m not trying to cheat!

581
00:27:40,333 --> 00:27:42,200
You wanted to cheat, but it didn’t work!

582
00:27:42,333 --> 00:27:44,000
(They laugh)

583
00:27:46,666 --> 00:27:47,166
Seven!

584
00:27:48,966 --> 00:27:50,400
Here’s another five and three,

585
00:27:50,433 --> 00:27:51,833
So justice is served!

586
00:27:51,866 --> 00:27:53,233
Agha Jan, you tell us!

587
00:27:53,266 --> 00:27:54,166
Was it five and two or five and three?

588
00:27:54,200 --> 00:27:55,400
Sir, you’re the witness,

589
00:27:55,433 --> 00:27:56,933
Was it five and two or five and three?

590
00:27:56,933 --> 00:27:58,733
Well, what can I say!

591
00:27:58,766 --> 00:28:00,000
If you have a conscience, tell the truth!

592
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:02,533
If I haven’t made a mistake, it was five and two!

593
00:28:02,566 --> 00:28:04,233
It was five and two… there you go!

594
00:28:04,266 --> 00:28:05,400
Didn’t I tell you?

595
00:28:06,100 --> 00:28:06,900
Oh, come off it! Leili, dear!

596
00:28:06,933 --> 00:28:08,033
Get up and bring a few walnuts,

597
00:28:08,033 --> 00:28:09,533
For Babajoon to play with!

598
00:28:09,633 --> 00:28:10,866
He doesn’t know what dice are!

599
00:28:10,866 --> 00:28:13,866
With lucky dice, anyone's a champion!

600
00:28:13,933 --> 00:28:14,666
Ouch!

601
00:28:14,666 --> 00:28:16,200
You don’t know how to play!

602
00:28:18,800 --> 00:28:20,233
They’ve started fighting again!

603
00:28:20,266 --> 00:28:23,700
You don’t know how to play, so why waste my time!

604
00:28:24,166 --> 00:28:26,166
Moment, Moment!

605
00:28:26,566 --> 00:28:27,533
Hands up!

606
00:28:27,566 --> 00:28:28,600
(Group laughter)

607
00:28:28,633 --> 00:28:30,133
Welcome! - Asadollah!

608
00:28:30,166 --> 00:28:31,900
You scared us!

609
00:28:34,266 --> 00:28:36,833
I said you’d probably forget to bring it for me again!

610
00:28:36,833 --> 00:28:38,066
Instead of a gun, I wanted

611
00:28:38,100 --> 00:28:39,933
To bring you a very beautiful girl!

612
00:28:40,700 --> 00:28:41,333
Brother!

613
00:28:41,333 --> 00:28:42,566
Let’s go to Uncle Asadollah. - Excuse me.

614
00:28:43,466 --> 00:28:44,833
Take a look at him.

615
00:28:44,966 --> 00:28:46,233
Take it.

616
00:28:46,266 --> 00:28:48,866
Look at you, you rascal,

617
00:28:49,500 --> 00:28:51,366
There you go again, barging

618
00:28:51,366 --> 00:28:53,066
Into people’s homes unannounced! - Well, well!

619
00:28:53,100 --> 00:28:55,500
My dear Mrs Aziz al-Saltaneh!

620
00:28:56,400 --> 00:28:58,000
Where’s that donkey Dustali?

621
00:28:58,066 --> 00:28:59,766
Catch your breath first, you clown,

622
00:28:59,800 --> 00:29:01,333
I’ll tell you later!

623
00:29:02,400 --> 00:29:03,000
You clown!

624
00:29:03,033 --> 00:29:05,000
Well! Everybody’s here!

625
00:29:05,033 --> 00:29:07,600
- He’s so lame, and so unfunny! - How can you say that?

626
00:29:07,600 --> 00:29:09,233
Hello, Dear Saeed! - What a splendid man!

627
00:29:09,766 --> 00:29:12,100
Leili’s all grown up! Turn around, let me see!

628
00:29:13,733 --> 00:29:14,300
(Sound of a scream)

629
00:29:14,300 --> 00:29:15,433
Make sure there’s no bullet in it!

630
00:29:15,466 --> 00:29:16,533
Oh, I’m scared!

631
00:29:16,533 --> 00:29:18,766
For God’s sake, tell Sir not to play with the gun!

632
00:29:20,466 --> 00:29:23,833
Don’t be afraid, Miss Farrokh Lagha!

633
00:29:23,833 --> 00:29:26,233
We grew up with guns!

634
00:29:26,266 --> 00:29:28,500
You naughty thing! Uncle Asadollah makes such jokes!

635
00:29:28,533 --> 00:29:30,066
Shazdeh Asadollah Mirza,

636
00:29:30,100 --> 00:29:32,300
The younger brother of Shamsali Mirza,

637
00:29:32,300 --> 00:29:34,300
And a member of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs,

638
00:29:34,333 --> 00:29:37,133
Had just returned from a mission in the Caucasus.

639
00:29:37,800 --> 00:29:40,533
For Shazdeh, nothing in the world was serious.

640
00:29:40,733 --> 00:29:43,366
Not even the hateful looks of husbands,

641
00:29:43,400 --> 00:29:45,633
When he teased their wives!

642
00:29:45,666 --> 00:29:46,900
So, how’s my Dear Aziz doing?

643
00:29:46,933 --> 00:29:47,433
You eat!

644
00:29:47,433 --> 00:29:48,600
You eat!

645
00:29:50,400 --> 00:29:51,700
Why are you wearing mourning clothes

646
00:29:51,733 --> 00:29:53,366
Even at a party, Farrokh Lagha!?

647
00:29:53,400 --> 00:29:53,933
None of your business!

648
00:29:54,833 --> 00:29:57,333
She’s looking more and more like an owl every day!

649
00:29:57,333 --> 00:29:58,566
Dustali, you’ve made this poor woman,

650
00:29:58,600 --> 00:30:00,266
Wear black for the rest of her life!

651
00:30:00,300 --> 00:30:02,466
Go for a San Francisco, bro!

652
00:30:03,766 --> 00:30:04,400
Agha jan,

653
00:30:04,433 --> 00:30:07,500
He wasn’t from a landed or aristocratic family.

654
00:30:07,600 --> 00:30:09,200
He was a licensed pharmacist,

655
00:30:09,233 --> 00:30:11,933
whom the pharmacy customers called “doctor.”

656
00:30:12,333 --> 00:30:13,466
Uncle Napoleon,

657
00:30:13,466 --> 00:30:16,433
considered his sister’s marriage to a non-aristocratic merchant,

658
00:30:16,433 --> 00:30:19,133
the greatest tragedy in history!

659
00:30:19,400 --> 00:30:21,033
Of course, that wasn’t very important.

660
00:30:21,066 --> 00:30:23,333
The real reason for the dispute between these two,

661
00:30:23,533 --> 00:30:26,333
was Napoleon Bonaparte, Emperor of France.

662
00:30:27,033 --> 00:30:29,133
Unlike Dear Uncle, Agha Jan

663
00:30:29,166 --> 00:30:31,600
considered Napoleon merely an adventurer,

664
00:30:31,633 --> 00:30:33,800
who had drenched Europe in blood.

665
00:30:35,866 --> 00:30:37,500
Why are you eating so much, girl?

666
00:30:37,533 --> 00:30:38,766
You’ll get sick!

667
00:30:39,233 --> 00:30:40,000
Aziz Khanum!

668
00:30:40,266 --> 00:30:41,833
Take care of this girl, please!

669
00:30:42,100 --> 00:30:45,633
Asadollah brought you a nice souvenir, bro.

670
00:30:46,200 --> 00:30:48,800
I had a gun just like this one myself.

671
00:30:49,433 --> 00:30:51,333
I remember one time,

672
00:30:51,333 --> 00:30:53,966
During the heat of the Mamasani war…

673
00:30:54,000 --> 00:30:57,066
No, Sir, no… it was the Kazerun war… yes!

674
00:30:58,033 --> 00:31:00,833
I’m saying it was during the Mamasani war!

675
00:31:00,866 --> 00:31:02,700
Why are you talking nonsense!

676
00:31:02,733 --> 00:31:03,966
Honestly, Sir, why should I lie!

677
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:05,466
As far as we remember,

678
00:31:05,500 --> 00:31:06,866
It was the Kazerun war!

679
00:31:06,866 --> 00:31:08,100
For God’s sake, man!

680
00:31:08,133 --> 00:31:11,966
One day during the heat of the Mamasani war!

681
00:31:12,766 --> 00:31:16,200
We were trapped in a valley during the war.

682
00:31:17,166 --> 00:31:20,300
The mountains on both sides

683
00:31:20,333 --> 00:31:22,800
Were held by armed bandits.

684
00:31:23,266 --> 00:31:26,333
It was a valley about

685
00:31:26,500 --> 00:31:30,533
Three or four times as wide as this room, and…

686
00:31:30,766 --> 00:31:32,000
It was me,

687
00:31:32,033 --> 00:31:34,133
And forty or fifty riflemen…

688
00:31:34,166 --> 00:31:35,533
And yours truly, Ghasem!

689
00:31:35,633 --> 00:31:36,533
Yes!

690
00:31:36,566 --> 00:31:39,433
This Ghasem was what they called back then

691
00:31:39,433 --> 00:31:40,533
My orderly.

692
00:31:40,533 --> 00:31:42,366
Didn’t we say, Sir, it was the Kazerun war?!

693
00:31:42,433 --> 00:31:45,233
It was the Mamasani war!

694
00:31:45,600 --> 00:31:48,700
It was me and forty or fifty riflemen!

695
00:31:48,866 --> 00:31:50,700
Now, these riflemen,

696
00:31:50,733 --> 00:31:54,633
What a sorry state they were in, never mind!

697
00:31:54,766 --> 00:31:56,400
As Napoleon said,

698
00:31:56,433 --> 00:32:00,433
One commander with a hundred well-fed soldiers,

699
00:32:00,733 --> 00:32:02,600
Can fight better,

700
00:32:02,833 --> 00:32:05,400
Than with a thousand hungry soldiers!

701
00:32:05,400 --> 00:32:05,900
That’s right!

702
00:32:06,400 --> 00:32:08,900
While we were under siege,

703
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:11,566
All of a sudden, a rain of bullets started!

704
00:32:11,600 --> 00:32:13,100
(Makes the sound of gunfire)

705
00:32:13,100 --> 00:32:16,700
The first thing I did,

706
00:32:17,666 --> 00:32:19,933
Was throw myself off the horse.

707
00:32:20,300 --> 00:32:22,266
Then I reached out,

708
00:32:22,333 --> 00:32:24,333
Grabbed someone or other by the waist…

709
00:32:24,366 --> 00:32:27,633
It seems it was Ghasem or someone else…

710
00:32:27,666 --> 00:32:29,333
And pulled him down!

711
00:32:29,466 --> 00:32:30,600
It was us, Sir!

712
00:32:30,666 --> 00:32:32,100
If we may be so bold,

713
00:32:32,100 --> 00:32:33,833
It was the Kazerun war!

714
00:32:34,200 --> 00:32:36,833
Whatever the hell it was!

715
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:39,933
Will you let me tell my story or not!?

716
00:32:40,900 --> 00:32:41,600
Very well, Sir!

717
00:32:41,600 --> 00:32:43,000
We know nothing at all.

718
00:32:43,033 --> 00:32:44,233
Our lips are sealed!

719
00:32:45,600 --> 00:32:46,966
This fool —

720
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:49,166
I wish I’d broken my hand

721
00:32:49,166 --> 00:32:51,400
Instead of saving him —

722
00:32:51,433 --> 00:32:53,400
I pulled him down from the horse.

723
00:32:54,533 --> 00:32:57,133
And what a situation it was,

724
00:32:58,166 --> 00:32:58,966
God only knows!

725
00:32:59,833 --> 00:33:02,766
Several of my men had been shot.

726
00:33:03,466 --> 00:33:05,566
I ordered the rest,

727
00:33:05,600 --> 00:33:08,500
To take position behind the boulders.

728
00:33:09,433 --> 00:33:13,733
From the way the enemy attacked and shot,

729
00:33:13,866 --> 00:33:15,900
I immediately realized,

730
00:33:15,933 --> 00:33:22,666
That we were facing the gang of the rebel Khodadad Khan!

731
00:33:24,933 --> 00:33:28,866
The same Khodadad Khan, the notorious rebel,

732
00:33:29,133 --> 00:33:32,200
Old servant of the English!

733
00:33:32,233 --> 00:33:34,700
Didn’t we say, Sir, it was the Kazerun war!?

734
00:33:34,833 --> 00:33:36,233
Shut up!

735
00:33:36,533 --> 00:33:38,033
(Group laughter)

736
00:33:38,133 --> 00:33:41,566
I told myself, one way or another,

737
00:33:41,566 --> 00:33:44,566
I had to finish off Khodadad Khan.

738
00:33:46,033 --> 00:33:47,633
These villains,

739
00:33:47,966 --> 00:33:52,233
As long as their leader is alive, they’re bold!

740
00:33:52,800 --> 00:33:56,100
As soon as their leader is killed,

741
00:33:56,100 --> 00:33:56,800
They flee!

742
00:33:57,966 --> 00:34:01,300
Crawling on my belly,

743
00:34:01,733 --> 00:34:05,333
I reached the top of that mountain!

744
00:34:05,766 --> 00:34:06,533
Up there!

745
00:34:09,300 --> 00:34:11,900
I had a fur hat on my head!

746
00:34:12,566 --> 00:34:13,933
No, no, no, no, no, no!

747
00:34:15,300 --> 00:34:18,766
I took the hat off my head,

748
00:34:18,766 --> 00:34:20,900
Put it on the tip of the bayonet,

749
00:34:20,933 --> 00:34:23,400
And raised the rifle.

750
00:34:23,433 --> 00:34:24,566
Didn’t we say, Sir!?

751
00:34:24,933 --> 00:34:27,366
In the Mamasani war, you didn’t have a fur hat!

752
00:34:27,933 --> 00:34:30,866
In the Kazerun war, when you were galloping on the horse,

753
00:34:30,900 --> 00:34:32,733
You lost your fur hat!

754
00:34:32,900 --> 00:34:34,700
No, no… I mean, it was shot!

755
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:38,233
In the Mamasani war, you didn’t have a fur hat at all!

756
00:34:40,233 --> 00:34:42,100
It seems Ghasem is right!

757
00:34:42,200 --> 00:34:44,200
W-W-W-Well, there you go!

758
00:34:44,733 --> 00:34:47,933
It was indeed the Kazerun war!

759
00:34:51,833 --> 00:34:52,766
I mean,

760
00:34:54,866 --> 00:34:57,000
It was the early days of the Kazerun war.

761
00:34:57,033 --> 00:34:59,200
Yes… there you go… there you go!

762
00:35:00,133 --> 00:35:03,700
The only thought in my head was,

763
00:35:03,733 --> 00:35:05,733
To shoot Khodadad Khan.

764
00:35:06,500 --> 00:35:11,000
As soon as I put the fur hat on the bayonet,

765
00:35:11,033 --> 00:35:12,966
And raised the rifle,

766
00:35:13,633 --> 00:35:19,166
Khodadad Khan, who was a top-notch shooter,

767
00:35:19,566 --> 00:35:23,200
Poked his head out from behind the boulders.

768
00:35:24,033 --> 00:35:26,833
Now it’s just me and him!

769
00:35:27,266 --> 00:35:32,533
I called on Imam Ali and held my breath.

770
00:35:34,300 --> 00:35:38,100
I was searching for Khodadad Khan’s forehead.

771
00:35:38,366 --> 00:35:41,266
I had seen his face from afar once.

772
00:35:41,400 --> 00:35:44,100
Bloodshot eyes!

773
00:35:44,200 --> 00:35:46,333
Thick eyebrows!

774
00:35:46,600 --> 00:35:50,833
I aimed between his two eyebrows and…

775
00:35:50,866 --> 00:35:54,733
(A sound like a fart)

776
00:35:54,766 --> 00:35:56,000
(Ghamar starts laughing)

777
00:35:56,133 --> 00:35:58,133
(The guests start laughing)

778
00:36:07,333 --> 00:36:08,666
Shut up!

779
00:36:09,700 --> 00:36:11,966
You rootless scoundrel!

780
00:36:13,800 --> 00:36:17,200
To raise up the lowborn

781
00:36:17,933 --> 00:36:21,300
And expect any good from them

782
00:36:22,033 --> 00:36:25,433
Is to lose your grip on your own affairs

783
00:36:25,566 --> 00:36:29,033
And nurse a viper in your bosom!

784
00:36:29,066 --> 00:36:29,733
(Sound of commotion)

785
00:36:29,766 --> 00:36:30,533
Ghasem!

786
00:36:30,566 --> 00:36:32,966
(Sound of commotion)

787
00:36:32,966 --> 00:36:34,733
Brother! Where are you going, Brother!

788
00:36:34,766 --> 00:36:35,666
Leili… home!

789
00:36:35,700 --> 00:36:37,900
Brother… you’re mistaken!

790
00:36:37,900 --> 00:36:40,166
Brother, please come back!

791
00:36:40,166 --> 00:36:40,533
Where are you going!

792
00:36:40,533 --> 00:36:42,766
It’s a misunderstanding, please come back!

793
00:36:42,800 --> 00:36:44,800
Why are you upset! - Brother… stay with us!

794
00:36:44,800 --> 00:36:46,966
Brother! Please!

795
00:36:47,000 --> 00:36:49,166
Alright, come on… he’s not going! - Come back!

796
00:36:49,200 --> 00:36:50,700
What’s that? What happened? What’s going on? Huh?

797
00:36:51,366 --> 00:36:52,400
Let’s go home!

798
00:36:52,400 --> 00:36:53,933
Oh! Why aren’t you talking?

799
00:36:55,566 --> 00:36:56,266
What’s happened?

800
00:36:56,300 --> 00:36:58,700
Tell me what’s going on? What’s the matter? - I’ll disgrace the lot of them!

801
00:36:58,700 --> 00:37:00,866
He accuses me? - Oh my God… keep your voice down!

802
00:37:00,900 --> 00:37:01,466
It’s embarrassing!

803
00:37:01,466 --> 00:37:02,233
Come, woman!

804
00:37:02,266 --> 00:37:02,866
Wait a minute!

805
00:37:02,900 --> 00:37:03,900
Let it go, now!

806
00:37:03,933 --> 00:37:04,500
What’s happened!

807
00:37:05,633 --> 00:37:07,333
Ladies and gentlemen, ladies!

808
00:37:07,366 --> 00:37:08,633
Please… please!

809
00:37:08,833 --> 00:37:09,700
It’s not a big deal.

810
00:37:09,733 --> 00:37:11,033
It’s a misunderstanding!

811
00:37:11,033 --> 00:37:12,866
Ladies and gentlemen!

812
00:37:12,900 --> 00:37:14,200
Now whoever it was, tell the truth!

813
00:37:14,233 --> 00:37:15,700
Who, in the middle of Sir’s story,

814
00:37:15,733 --> 00:37:16,600
Fired off a shot?

815
00:37:16,633 --> 00:37:17,766
(Group laughter)

816
00:37:17,966 --> 00:37:19,866
Whatever else, he’s our elder brother.

817
00:37:19,866 --> 00:37:21,266
I beg you, dear.

818
00:37:21,300 --> 00:37:22,400
Let it go.

819
00:37:23,033 --> 00:37:26,000
I’ll show him a Kazerun war he’ll never forget!

820
00:37:34,033 --> 00:37:35,200
He recites poetry at me,

821
00:37:35,233 --> 00:37:37,733
“To raise up the lowborn”!?

822
00:37:38,500 --> 00:37:40,066
I’ll pull such a Napoleon on him

823
00:37:40,100 --> 00:37:42,200
That seven Napoleons will come pouring out of him!

824
00:37:50,700 --> 00:37:52,500
The turmoil of first love

825
00:37:52,533 --> 00:37:54,700
Had not yet subsided in my heart,

826
00:37:54,733 --> 00:37:55,900
When the fear of war,

827
00:37:56,233 --> 00:37:58,933
Cast a shadow over the large garden of the house.

828
00:37:59,533 --> 00:38:00,166
That night,

829
00:38:00,533 --> 00:38:02,633
In the maddening silence of the garden,

830
00:38:02,900 --> 00:38:04,833
Everyone, even the flowers and trees,

831
00:38:04,866 --> 00:38:06,300
Were awaiting a war,

832
00:38:06,600 --> 00:38:09,033
More ruthless than the first world war!

833
00:38:09,666 --> 00:38:12,300
The war of Agha Jan and Dear Uncle Napoleon!

834
00:38:14,966 --> 00:38:17,900
♪ Traditional music ♪

835
00:38:18,066 --> 00:38:20,833
In those years, there was still no piped water.

836
00:38:21,066 --> 00:38:23,000
Once a month, the water master

837
00:38:23,033 --> 00:38:24,600
Would divert water to our house,

838
00:38:24,633 --> 00:38:27,133
And through the channels in the garden,

839
00:38:27,233 --> 00:38:29,700
We would fill the pools and water reservoirs.

840
00:38:30,500 --> 00:38:31,833
The water from the first alley

841
00:38:31,866 --> 00:38:34,233
would flow into the pool in Uncle Napoleon's courtyard,

842
00:38:34,366 --> 00:38:36,566
and from there, it would reach our house.

843
00:38:37,233 --> 00:38:40,466
On Dear Uncle’s orders, Mash Ghasem

844
00:38:40,600 --> 00:38:43,233
Dammed the channel where it entered our house,

845
00:38:43,566 --> 00:38:45,566
And he, like a brave officer,

846
00:38:45,666 --> 00:38:46,766
Stood guard.

847
00:38:47,100 --> 00:38:49,833
♪ Traditional music ♪

848
00:38:55,500 --> 00:38:57,066
Cutting off our house’s water,

849
00:38:57,100 --> 00:39:00,233
Was equivalent to cutting off Dear Uncle Colonel’s water.

850
00:39:00,400 --> 00:39:03,300
Because the water went from our house to their reservoir.

851
00:39:03,533 --> 00:39:04,633
In this dispute,

852
00:39:04,666 --> 00:39:06,000
Poor Dear Uncle Colonel,

853
00:39:06,033 --> 00:39:08,133
Whose garden’s flowers and trees,

854
00:39:08,166 --> 00:39:11,100
Were being sacrificed to the conflict between Agha Jan and Dear Uncle.

855
00:39:11,533 --> 00:39:14,033
♪ Traditional music ♪

856
00:39:19,966 --> 00:39:21,566
Mash Ghasem, where are the kids?

857
00:39:21,600 --> 00:39:22,700
Didn’t they come to the garden today?

858
00:39:23,033 --> 00:39:24,666
Honestly, kid, why should I lie!

859
00:39:24,866 --> 00:39:26,800
Truth is, we’re not supposed to talk to you!

860
00:39:26,933 --> 00:39:27,566
Why?!

861
00:39:28,066 --> 00:39:29,166
Don’t you see?

862
00:39:29,266 --> 00:39:30,466
We’re on sentry duty.

863
00:39:34,800 --> 00:39:35,666
Mash Ghasem!

864
00:39:36,233 --> 00:39:37,266
Leili didn’t come either?

865
00:39:37,866 --> 00:39:39,366
Honestly, we don’t know anything.

866
00:39:40,166 --> 00:39:42,766
But it could be that Sir told Miss Leili,

867
00:39:42,800 --> 00:39:45,400
That she doesn’t have the right to step out of the house.

868
00:39:45,433 --> 00:39:46,333
Why, Mash Ghasem?

869
00:39:47,800 --> 00:39:50,366
Weren’t you at Mr. Colonel’s house last night?

870
00:39:50,766 --> 00:39:52,533
Kid, didn’t you see what happened?

871
00:39:53,800 --> 00:39:55,333
Did Dear Uncle get very angry?

872
00:39:56,366 --> 00:39:57,700
Honestly, kid, why should I lie!

873
00:39:58,233 --> 00:39:59,433
Since morning until now,

874
00:39:59,466 --> 00:40:01,300
We haven’t seen Sir with our own eyes,

875
00:40:02,033 --> 00:40:04,866
But we heard his voice from the room with our own ears.

876
00:40:05,533 --> 00:40:07,566
Like a wounded lion!

877
00:40:08,766 --> 00:40:10,566
And honestly, kid, Sir has a point!

878
00:40:11,766 --> 00:40:14,000
When the talk is about the Kazerun war,

879
00:40:14,000 --> 00:40:15,566
And that happens mid-story?!

880
00:40:16,633 --> 00:40:18,966
Now, if it was the Mamasani war, that’s one thing!

881
00:40:19,200 --> 00:40:21,266
But when the talk is about the Kazerun war,

882
00:40:21,266 --> 00:40:22,333
It’s not a joking matter!

883
00:40:22,866 --> 00:40:24,266
We ourselves, with our own eyes,

884
00:40:24,266 --> 00:40:25,700
Saw what Sir did!

885
00:40:26,700 --> 00:40:29,033
The peace and safety in the province today

886
00:40:29,066 --> 00:40:30,266
Is all thanks to Sir!

887
00:40:31,700 --> 00:40:33,233
God give him long life.

888
00:40:34,066 --> 00:40:36,433
When he rode his chestnut horse,

889
00:40:36,433 --> 00:40:39,333
And galloped in the battlefield with a sword in hand,

890
00:40:40,333 --> 00:40:42,433
He was like a charging lion!

891
00:40:43,366 --> 00:40:45,500
Even we, on his own side,

892
00:40:45,533 --> 00:40:47,300
Were scared out of our wits!

893
00:40:47,333 --> 00:40:48,300
Let alone the enemy!

894
00:40:48,333 --> 00:40:49,033
Now, Mash Ghasem!

895
00:40:49,033 --> 00:40:50,166
Do you think that sound last night…

896
00:40:50,200 --> 00:40:51,333
Yes, kid!

897
00:40:51,366 --> 00:40:52,500
It was him!

898
00:40:52,866 --> 00:40:53,933
Why should I lie?

899
00:40:54,033 --> 00:40:55,833
The grave is this close!

900
00:40:56,833 --> 00:40:58,566
We didn’t hear it with our own ears.

901
00:40:58,600 --> 00:40:59,666
I mean, we did hear!

902
00:40:59,700 --> 00:41:01,733
But our attention was on Sir’s words,

903
00:41:01,766 --> 00:41:02,600
And the gunfire!

904
00:41:02,933 --> 00:41:05,133
We’ve heard these sounds plenty before!

905
00:41:05,433 --> 00:41:07,733
It’s a sound you can hear even

906
00:41:07,766 --> 00:41:08,666
Over cannon and rifle fire!

907
00:41:09,666 --> 00:41:11,933
But this time, Sir heard it with his own ears!

908
00:41:12,800 --> 00:41:15,433
And honestly, when we were walking home with Sir,

909
00:41:15,466 --> 00:41:17,566
Master Pouri stirred up a lot of trouble, too!

910
00:41:18,166 --> 00:41:20,033
Did Pouri come to Dear Uncle’s house too?

911
00:41:20,166 --> 00:41:22,533
Yes, kid! He came as far as the door!

912
00:41:22,733 --> 00:41:24,033
I mean, he came in too!

913
00:41:24,500 --> 00:41:25,933
And he kept whispering in Sir’s ear,

914
00:41:25,966 --> 00:41:28,166
That Sir had been disrespected!

915
00:41:29,800 --> 00:41:31,100
But why, Mash Ghasem?!

916
00:41:31,133 --> 00:41:32,366
What does Pouri gain,

917
00:41:32,366 --> 00:41:34,233
From a fight and quarrel between Dear Uncle and Agha Jan?

918
00:41:34,266 --> 00:41:36,533
Honestly, kid, if you ask us,

919
00:41:36,566 --> 00:41:38,900
Master Pouri is sweet on Miss Leili!

920
00:41:39,333 --> 00:41:41,466
He even sent his mother once,

921
00:41:41,500 --> 00:41:43,200
To propose to Miss Leili!

922
00:41:43,600 --> 00:41:46,166
And last night, when you were playing with Miss Leili,

923
00:41:46,200 --> 00:41:47,800
He was very jealous.

924
00:41:48,400 --> 00:41:49,933
Doesn’t he know that Miss Leili

925
00:41:49,933 --> 00:41:52,366
Is thirteen or fourteen, she kan get married,

926
00:41:52,600 --> 00:41:53,333
But kid!

927
00:41:53,366 --> 00:41:55,100
You, who are fourteen or fifteen years old,

928
00:41:55,100 --> 00:41:56,533
You kan’t get married!

929
00:41:59,400 --> 00:42:00,100
Mash Ghasem!

930
00:42:05,266 --> 00:42:07,933
In all the love stories I had read,

931
00:42:08,133 --> 00:42:11,100
There was one lover, one beloved, and one rival!

932
00:42:11,666 --> 00:42:12,833
It was strange that I had never,

933
00:42:12,866 --> 00:42:14,600
Thought of a rival!

934
00:42:15,266 --> 00:42:16,400
Now I was slowly beginning to understand

935
00:42:16,433 --> 00:42:17,833
Why from the very first day,

936
00:42:17,966 --> 00:42:19,733
I had feared love for no reason!

937
00:42:24,066 --> 00:42:24,800
Mash Ghasem!

938
00:42:24,833 --> 00:42:25,333
Hum!

939
00:42:26,266 --> 00:42:28,200
Last night, did you block our water?

940
00:42:28,366 --> 00:42:30,266
Well, Mr. Colonel, it just sort of happened!

941
00:42:30,600 --> 00:42:31,500
Happened how?

942
00:42:31,633 --> 00:42:33,133
What does “it just happened” mean?

943
00:42:33,766 --> 00:42:35,966
Honestly, why lie! We don’ know nothin’!

944
00:42:36,166 --> 00:42:37,700
What does “we don’t know” mean?

945
00:42:38,033 --> 00:42:40,166
You blocked the water and now you don’ know?

946
00:42:40,300 --> 00:42:42,033
When did we block your water?

947
00:42:42,066 --> 00:42:43,933
We blocked the water of your sister’s husband!

948
00:42:44,066 --> 00:42:46,733
The water’s gotta come from Mr. Doctor’s house to ours!

949
00:42:46,766 --> 00:42:48,466
Don’t come any closer, Mr. Colonel, don’t come closer!

950
00:42:49,366 --> 00:42:50,633
Sure, you’re a colonel,

951
00:42:50,666 --> 00:42:52,200
But we’re on sentry duty here!

952
00:42:52,733 --> 00:42:54,400
Sir gave orders like this!

953
00:42:55,500 --> 00:42:57,000
Even if it costs us our life,

954
00:42:57,033 --> 00:42:58,533
We won’t let the water go from this side to that!

955
00:42:58,566 --> 00:42:59,700
You mean to say,

956
00:43:00,466 --> 00:43:02,800
Sir told you to cut off our water?

957
00:43:02,833 --> 00:43:04,166
This mornin’ Sir himself said,

958
00:43:04,200 --> 00:43:06,366
Ghasem, you stand here,

959
00:43:06,400 --> 00:43:08,100
Don’t let anyone touch this dam!

960
00:43:08,733 --> 00:43:11,333
Whoever comes, you hit ’em in the head with this shovel!

961
00:43:11,600 --> 00:43:13,033
Go! Don't stand there! Uh…

962
00:43:24,166 --> 00:43:26,100
I wanna slap him right in the face.

963
00:43:26,333 --> 00:43:27,200
In whose face?

964
00:43:28,200 --> 00:43:29,566
Mr. Colonel!?

965
00:43:29,600 --> 00:43:30,966
No, in Pouri’s face!

966
00:43:31,000 --> 00:43:32,333
With that long face of his!

967
00:43:32,600 --> 00:43:34,533
Sure, Master Pouri is a bit dim,

968
00:43:34,533 --> 00:43:36,733
But he’s a snake in the grass!

969
00:43:38,066 --> 00:43:38,900
Mash Ghasem!

970
00:43:38,933 --> 00:43:41,100
In your opinion, will Leili become Pouri’s wife?

971
00:43:41,533 --> 00:43:42,500
Honestly, kid!

972
00:43:42,533 --> 00:43:44,633
Miss Leili is a girl of marrying age.

973
00:43:44,933 --> 00:43:46,266
And Master Pouri, granted,

974
00:43:46,266 --> 00:43:47,866
Is a bit of a mama’s boy and a dimwit!

975
00:43:48,133 --> 00:43:49,666
But he’s finished his studies.

976
00:43:50,000 --> 00:43:51,433
And cousins like those,

977
00:43:51,466 --> 00:43:54,300
Are a match made in heaven!

978
00:43:54,500 --> 00:43:56,466
Can you tell Leili to come to the garden for a bit?

979
00:43:56,933 --> 00:43:58,933
You kids will be the death of me!

980
00:43:59,266 --> 00:44:00,033
If Sir finds out,

981
00:44:00,066 --> 00:44:02,366
We took your message to Miss Leili,

982
00:44:02,400 --> 00:44:04,600
He’ll roast us all alive!

983
00:44:05,533 --> 00:44:07,266
Alright, never mind for now.

984
00:44:07,966 --> 00:44:09,166
Fine, another day then.

985
00:44:17,566 --> 00:44:19,400
From the very first day,

986
00:44:19,400 --> 00:44:22,133
I was against his marriage to our sister.

987
00:44:22,366 --> 00:44:23,733
It was your fault.

988
00:44:23,833 --> 00:44:26,666
Brother, don’t blow this out of proportion.

989
00:44:26,966 --> 00:44:30,433
This war and quarrel is all the result of a misunderstanding.

990
00:44:30,466 --> 00:44:32,466
Misunderstanding? More like indigestion!

991
00:44:33,000 --> 00:44:35,566
Making that noise in the middle of my story?

992
00:44:35,566 --> 00:44:37,933
I’ll skin that wretch alive!

993
00:44:37,966 --> 00:44:41,733
I’ll run him out of this town.

994
00:44:41,966 --> 00:44:44,866
What a pity for our dear sister,

995
00:44:44,900 --> 00:44:47,233
Who became the wife of this vile man!

996
00:44:48,100 --> 00:44:49,400
You’re the head of the family.

997
00:44:49,433 --> 00:44:50,733
You are our elder.

998
00:44:50,966 --> 00:44:53,300
Be magnanimous and forgive him.

999
00:44:53,733 --> 00:44:55,433
It’s not good for people to know,

1000
00:44:55,433 --> 00:44:58,533
You cut off the water to your own family!

1001
00:44:58,966 --> 00:45:01,633
There’s not a drop of water in our reservoir.

1002
00:45:01,666 --> 00:45:03,933
Our trees are dying of thirst.

1003
00:45:04,433 --> 00:45:06,933
Hurry up and get out of here! - You’ve had a dispute with your sister’s husband,

1004
00:45:06,966 --> 00:45:08,366
Babajoon said if I talk to you - Why do you cut off our water?

1005
00:45:08,400 --> 00:45:09,533
He’ll set the whole house on fire!

1006
00:45:09,533 --> 00:45:11,800
Leili… Leili! - Maybe it’s your sister’s husband,

1007
00:45:11,833 --> 00:45:13,033
Do you know what Mash Ghasem was sayin’?

1008
00:45:13,066 --> 00:45:14,633
- But my sister’s husband, never!

1009
00:45:14,666 --> 00:45:15,833
Saeed, get out of here!

1010
00:45:15,866 --> 00:45:18,766
- Go tell our sister to get a divorce…

1011
00:45:18,766 --> 00:45:19,566
Mash Ghasem was sayin’,

1012
00:45:19,600 --> 00:45:21,466
Pouri wants to send his mother to propose!

1013
00:45:21,500 --> 00:45:22,533
Propose for me?!

1014
00:45:22,566 --> 00:45:23,700
- Don’t turn me down.

1015
00:45:23,900 --> 00:45:25,000
Mash Ghasem was sayin’!

1016
00:45:25,333 --> 00:45:27,133
Mash Ghasem said Pouri loves you.

1017
00:45:27,133 --> 00:45:27,666
- Please,

1018
00:45:27,666 --> 00:45:29,200
Well, if it’s true, what’ll you do?

1019
00:45:29,233 --> 00:45:30,766
Me?! Me?! - Go tell him Sir said,

1020
00:45:30,800 --> 00:45:32,833
- He should come here himself and apologize to me!

1021
00:45:33,700 --> 00:45:37,100
(Leili cries) ♪ Sad music ♪

1022
00:45:41,566 --> 00:45:42,933
When Leili cried,

1023
00:45:42,966 --> 00:45:45,566
I finally realized what a foolish thing I’d done!

1024
00:45:45,966 --> 00:45:48,500
Before I confessed my own love to her,

1025
00:45:48,900 --> 00:45:50,800
I’d become a tool for the rival’s love,

1026
00:45:50,833 --> 00:45:52,233
To reach the beloved’s ears!

1027
00:45:52,700 --> 00:45:54,500
With this mistake, I understood that love,

1028
00:45:54,800 --> 00:45:56,433
Sometimes makes a person foolish.

1029
00:45:56,766 --> 00:46:00,033
Everyone knows that sound wasn’t from you.

1030
00:46:00,866 --> 00:46:02,533
But Brother is being stubborn!

1031
00:46:02,533 --> 00:46:03,866
He's just stubborn!

1032
00:46:05,833 --> 00:46:07,400
Now you be the bigger person,

1033
00:46:07,433 --> 00:46:09,433
Just pop over and apologize to him,

1034
00:46:09,466 --> 00:46:11,166
So maybe these disputes will end.

1035
00:46:11,200 --> 00:46:12,300
Me apologize?!

1036
00:46:12,766 --> 00:46:14,100
He insulted me,

1037
00:46:14,133 --> 00:46:15,466
And I should apologize to him?!

1038
00:46:15,733 --> 00:46:17,966
What Sir did,

1039
00:46:18,133 --> 00:46:21,266
Reminds you of the siege of Karbala!

1040
00:46:21,300 --> 00:46:23,500
Is he Shimr, cutting off water to the people!?

1041
00:46:23,566 --> 00:46:24,066
Huh?

1042
00:46:25,933 --> 00:46:27,300
Everyone knows I came,

1043
00:46:27,333 --> 00:46:29,033
To beg you to make peace.

1044
00:46:29,066 --> 00:46:32,033
Tell him if he insists on cutting off the water,

1045
00:46:32,066 --> 00:46:33,633
With the courts and the police,

1046
00:46:33,633 --> 00:46:35,433
I’ll give him what he deserves!

1047
00:46:35,466 --> 00:46:36,200
The court?

1048
00:46:36,966 --> 00:46:38,266
The police?

1049
00:46:39,066 --> 00:46:40,933
Oh, what a calamity!

1050
00:46:43,433 --> 00:46:44,900
Two whole days passed

1051
00:46:44,933 --> 00:46:46,633
Without my seeing Leili.

1052
00:46:48,066 --> 00:46:50,466
Comings and goings and diplomatic talks,

1053
00:46:50,466 --> 00:46:54,333
For a peaceful resolution of the dispute and ending the water shortage,

1054
00:46:54,366 --> 00:46:55,900
Had become so numerous,

1055
00:46:55,933 --> 00:46:58,366
That I had forgotten my own grief and pain.

1056
00:46:59,400 --> 00:47:00,600
Not even a drop of water,

1057
00:47:00,633 --> 00:47:03,000
Remained in Dear Uncle Colonel’s reservoir.

1058
00:47:03,033 --> 00:47:03,966
- Shazdeh has arrived.

1059
00:47:03,966 --> 00:47:05,866
Agha Jan didn’t make the slightest protest.

1060
00:47:05,900 --> 00:47:07,033
By his order,

1061
00:47:07,066 --> 00:47:09,466
Water in our house was rationed,

1062
00:47:09,466 --> 00:47:10,533
And for this reason,

1063
00:47:10,566 --> 00:47:13,366
We still had a little water stored in the reservoir.

1064
00:47:14,466 --> 00:47:15,666
All hopes were pinned

1065
00:47:15,700 --> 00:47:17,466
On the efforts

1066
00:47:17,466 --> 00:47:18,500
Of Dear Uncle Colonel.

1067
00:47:18,666 --> 00:47:20,933
His fate in the water crisis,

1068
00:47:20,933 --> 00:47:23,333
Was entirely tied to our fate.

1069
00:47:23,366 --> 00:47:24,700
- Please close that door.

1070
00:47:24,700 --> 00:47:26,166
Go to the kids.

1071
00:47:26,700 --> 00:47:27,266
- Please.

1072
00:47:27,300 --> 00:47:29,633
- Come in… no need for ‘please’!

1073
00:47:29,666 --> 00:47:30,566
Come in!

1074
00:47:30,600 --> 00:47:32,100
- Ladies, gentlemen!

1075
00:47:33,366 --> 00:47:34,833
From this situation that’s arisen,

1076
00:47:34,866 --> 00:47:37,933
The late Great Sir must be turning in his grave.

1077
00:47:39,233 --> 00:47:40,633
I did everything I could,

1078
00:47:40,700 --> 00:47:43,633
To preserve the unity of this old family,

1079
00:47:43,666 --> 00:47:44,866
I tried hard.

1080
00:47:44,966 --> 00:47:47,733
I even begged them both on my knees!

1081
00:47:48,033 --> 00:47:49,533
But neither Brother,

1082
00:47:50,033 --> 00:47:51,466
Nor my sister’s husband,

1083
00:47:51,500 --> 00:47:53,366
Would get off his high horse!

1084
00:47:53,933 --> 00:47:56,166
Now I’ve turned to you for help,

1085
00:47:56,633 --> 00:47:57,966
To do something

1086
00:47:58,000 --> 00:48:02,400
To preserve the sacred, centuries-old unity of this family.

1087
00:48:04,300 --> 00:48:05,733
Mr. Shamsali Mirza!

1088
00:48:05,866 --> 00:48:09,133
Please don’t let the police and the court,

1089
00:48:09,166 --> 00:48:10,433
Get involved here again!

1090
00:48:10,466 --> 00:48:11,366
Yes!

1091
00:48:11,366 --> 00:48:15,233
I thank the ladies and gentlemen,

1092
00:48:15,266 --> 00:48:17,466
Who have honored me.

1093
00:48:17,866 --> 00:48:21,700
As the chair of the meeting, I must say that I,

1094
00:48:21,833 --> 00:48:24,000
Since the establishment of the court,

1095
00:48:24,966 --> 00:48:28,733
Have served as an interrogator in the court.

1096
00:48:29,700 --> 00:48:32,733
I consider investigation and interrogation,

1097
00:48:32,766 --> 00:48:35,800
The key to solving any issue,

1098
00:48:36,066 --> 00:48:38,066
Be it political,

1099
00:48:38,100 --> 00:48:39,233
Social,

1100
00:48:39,266 --> 00:48:42,766
Familial, and so on and so forth!

1101
00:48:43,033 --> 00:48:45,566
For this reason, I propose that,

1102
00:48:45,800 --> 00:48:48,000
Before anything else,

1103
00:48:48,366 --> 00:48:51,033
It must be clarified that

1104
00:48:51,033 --> 00:48:57,000
That suspicious sound at Mr. Colonel’s party night,

1105
00:48:57,166 --> 00:48:59,600
Which gave rise

1106
00:48:59,633 --> 00:49:02,100
To all these disputes,

1107
00:49:02,533 --> 00:49:05,933
Did it have a human origin,

1108
00:49:06,533 --> 00:49:07,900
Or a non-human one?

1109
00:49:08,300 --> 00:49:09,300
Secondly!

1110
00:49:10,433 --> 00:49:11,966
If

1111
00:49:13,133 --> 00:49:16,233
It had a human origin,

1112
00:49:16,433 --> 00:49:19,533
It must be determined whether,

1113
00:49:20,233 --> 00:49:23,533
It came from your sister’s husband,

1114
00:49:23,800 --> 00:49:26,866
That is, Mr. Doctor! - Oh, the shame of it!

1115
00:49:26,900 --> 00:49:27,933
Or not!

1116
00:49:28,200 --> 00:49:29,200
Thirdly!

1117
00:49:30,166 --> 00:49:35,200
If it was from your sister’s husband,

1118
00:49:35,800 --> 00:49:38,000
Was it intentional or unintentional!

1119
00:49:38,000 --> 00:49:40,200
If it turns out the sound did come from Mr. Doctor,

1120
00:49:40,233 --> 00:49:41,133
The feud will only get worse!

1121
00:49:41,166 --> 00:49:42,666
Yes, it’ll get much worse!

1122
00:49:42,700 --> 00:49:46,433
Quiet! Quiet! Quiet! (Crowd murmurs)

1123
00:49:46,466 --> 00:49:48,400
Allow me! Mrs Aziz al-Saltaneh,

1124
00:49:48,433 --> 00:49:50,433
You’re absolutely right. - Thank you!

1125
00:49:50,466 --> 00:49:54,233
We held this meeting to maybe reconcile them!

1126
00:49:54,233 --> 00:49:56,000
Not to make them worse,

1127
00:49:56,033 --> 00:49:57,666
And set them against each other! - Very well… Please allow me!

1128
00:49:57,700 --> 00:49:59,900
(Crowd murmurs) Moment… Moment-

1129
00:49:59,900 --> 00:50:02,566
If the court isn’t seeking the truth, (Crowd murmurs)

1130
00:50:03,200 --> 00:50:07,000
Then with the permission of the ladies and gentlemen,

1131
00:50:07,033 --> 00:50:08,333
I’ll take my leave! - Where are you going!

1132
00:50:08,366 --> 00:50:10,133
(Crowd murmurs) - Please!

1133
00:50:10,166 --> 00:50:11,866
If we said something, we didn’t mean any harm! (Crowd murmurs)

1134
00:50:11,900 --> 00:50:13,200
Ladies and gentlemen! - Yes, we didn’t mean anything.

1135
00:50:13,700 --> 00:50:14,533
Whatever else, brother,

1136
00:50:14,566 --> 00:50:16,400
He’s a court interrogator, suspended or not!

1137
00:50:16,433 --> 00:50:17,500
We’re not experts!

1138
00:50:17,533 --> 00:50:19,033
Brother, don’t take offense.

1139
00:50:19,066 --> 00:50:19,700
- Please!

1140
00:50:19,700 --> 00:50:21,100
We agree with your investigation! (Crowd murmurs)

1141
00:50:21,133 --> 00:50:21,966
- Yes! We completely agree!

1142
00:50:22,000 --> 00:50:23,300
Bless you!

1143
00:50:23,333 --> 00:50:25,933
Please! I mean, everyone’s pleading! (Crowd murmurs)

1144
00:50:25,966 --> 00:50:27,266
- Please go on, Your Highness!

1145
00:50:27,266 --> 00:50:28,633
Please, go on!

1146
00:50:32,233 --> 00:50:35,933
Therefore, I will raise my first question.

1147
00:50:36,633 --> 00:50:37,833
All of you,

1148
00:50:37,833 --> 00:50:41,533
Who were present at that night’s party,

1149
00:50:41,566 --> 00:50:44,133
Did that suspicious sound,

1150
00:50:44,166 --> 00:50:47,400
Have a human or non-human origin?

1151
00:50:47,700 --> 00:50:48,733
Human!

1152
00:50:49,700 --> 00:50:50,800
Non-human!

1153
00:50:50,833 --> 00:50:52,333
It was like the sound of a chair.

1154
00:50:52,333 --> 00:50:53,766
Moment, Moment, Moment

1155
00:50:54,566 --> 00:50:57,866
I’m torn between human and chair.

1156
00:50:57,900 --> 00:50:59,266
Bless you!

1157
00:50:59,300 --> 00:51:01,866
I’m a bit hard of hearing.

1158
00:51:01,900 --> 00:51:03,766
I didn’t hear it clearly.

1159
00:51:03,766 --> 00:51:05,000
Quiet, quiet!

1160
00:51:05,033 --> 00:51:06,366
Ladies and gentlemen!

1161
00:51:06,400 --> 00:51:06,866
Silence!

1162
00:51:06,866 --> 00:51:09,866
Now that no one knows if that suspicious sound,

1163
00:51:09,900 --> 00:51:13,533
Had a human or non-human origin,

1164
00:51:13,900 --> 00:51:18,366
I will now raise a sub-question

1165
00:51:18,400 --> 00:51:19,200
Related to the first main question!

1166
00:51:19,233 --> 00:51:20,066
- Go ahead!

1167
00:51:20,266 --> 00:51:21,633
We need to see,

1168
00:51:21,766 --> 00:51:26,066
Who was seated near the spot

1169
00:51:26,100 --> 00:51:27,166
Where the suspicious sound occurred!

1170
00:51:27,366 --> 00:51:29,333
Sir! Sir himself!

1171
00:51:29,400 --> 00:51:31,733
No! No! He won’t show up here!

1172
00:51:31,766 --> 00:51:32,600
Doctor!

1173
00:51:32,633 --> 00:51:34,033
Your sister’s husband!

1174
00:51:34,066 --> 00:51:35,200
He won’t come either!

1175
00:51:35,233 --> 00:51:36,333
He’s dug his heels in!

1176
00:51:36,366 --> 00:51:37,900
I talked to him at length.

1177
00:51:37,933 --> 00:51:39,066
He won’t agree no matter what!

1178
00:51:39,066 --> 00:51:39,933
Ghamar!

1179
00:51:40,066 --> 00:51:41,466
Miss Ghamar!

1180
00:51:41,500 --> 00:51:43,233
Daughter of Mrs Aziz al-Saltaneh!

1181
00:51:43,500 --> 00:51:44,000
Yes!

1182
00:51:44,000 --> 00:51:44,500
Yes!

1183
00:51:44,566 --> 00:51:45,500
Yes, Uncle Asadollah?

1184
00:51:45,533 --> 00:51:46,833
Did you call me?

1185
00:51:47,000 --> 00:51:49,266
No, dear! No, bless you!

1186
00:51:49,766 --> 00:51:50,600
Go outside.

1187
00:51:50,600 --> 00:51:52,066
We just said your name, that’s all!

1188
00:51:52,666 --> 00:51:53,600
- Yes!

1189
00:51:54,100 --> 00:51:56,233
Bless you!

1190
00:51:56,266 --> 00:51:58,166
Bless you!

1191
00:51:59,666 --> 00:52:01,100
It wouldn’t have hurt if she sat here.

1192
00:52:01,133 --> 00:52:02,900
Ghamar is still a child. - Oh! What do you mean, it wouldn’t hurt?!

1193
00:52:02,933 --> 00:52:05,366
What does a child know about interrogation?

1194
00:52:05,400 --> 00:52:06,766
True! - Mrs Aziz is right!

1195
00:52:06,800 --> 00:52:08,033
Then you tell me,

1196
00:52:08,033 --> 00:52:10,166
Who should I interrogate?

1197
00:52:10,200 --> 00:52:11,166
Wait!

1198
00:52:12,566 --> 00:52:14,233
If you recall,

1199
00:52:14,466 --> 00:52:16,933
That night, next to Brother,

1200
00:52:17,333 --> 00:52:19,100
Mash Ghasem was there too!

1201
00:52:19,333 --> 00:52:21,133
Mash Ghasem wasn’t next to Sir,

1202
00:52:21,133 --> 00:52:22,466
He was behind Sir!

1203
00:52:22,500 --> 00:52:25,533
Now, Sir didn’t have a sound direction finder!

1204
00:52:26,133 --> 00:52:27,000
I propose,

1205
00:52:27,000 --> 00:52:28,733
We send someone to get Mash Ghasem!

1206
00:52:29,400 --> 00:52:31,300
If we don’t get results from the investigation,

1207
00:52:31,333 --> 00:52:33,333
We need to somehow convince Mash Ghasem

1208
00:52:33,400 --> 00:52:35,300
To say the sound came from him!

1209
00:52:35,700 --> 00:52:37,300
Sir will believe him.

1210
00:52:37,700 --> 00:52:39,733
This way… maybe the fight will be settled!

1211
00:52:39,766 --> 00:52:42,166
This Mash Ghasem, I know him well.

1212
00:52:42,233 --> 00:52:42,533
Well?!

1213
00:52:42,533 --> 00:52:44,166
He’s not one to go along with it.

1214
00:52:44,566 --> 00:52:45,633
He considers that kind of sound

1215
00:52:45,666 --> 00:52:47,566
A matter of honor!

1216
00:52:48,066 --> 00:52:49,866
If you give him a good sum of money,

1217
00:52:49,900 --> 00:52:51,100
He might agree!

1218
00:52:51,133 --> 00:52:52,733
Mash Ghasem isn’t swayed by money!

1219
00:52:52,766 --> 00:52:54,400
Mash Ghasem was saying a while ago,

1220
00:52:54,433 --> 00:52:55,966
He only has one wish!

1221
00:52:56,000 --> 00:52:59,466
He wishes to build a reservoir in Ghias Abad, Qom,

1222
00:52:59,500 --> 00:53:00,700
And dedicate it to the people!

1223
00:53:00,700 --> 00:53:02,300
That’s it! - Well done!

1224
00:53:02,333 --> 00:53:03,533
Well done!

1225
00:53:03,566 --> 00:53:05,366
Bless you!

1226
00:53:05,400 --> 00:53:07,000
It was a reasonable proposal!

1227
00:53:07,033 --> 00:53:08,700
I very much doubt

1228
00:53:08,733 --> 00:53:10,033
That Mash Ghasem will agree!

1229
00:53:10,566 --> 00:53:13,033
We gotta find a way to convince him then! - Why!

1230
00:53:13,433 --> 00:53:15,766
Building a reservoir ain’t cheap!

1231
00:53:15,800 --> 00:53:16,733
We’ll tell him,

1232
00:53:16,766 --> 00:53:19,666
In return, God’ll be pleased with his deeds in the next world!

1233
00:53:19,700 --> 00:53:22,433
Make his reservoir a handspan bigger,

1234
00:53:22,466 --> 00:53:23,466
He’ll agree!

1235
00:53:26,966 --> 00:53:29,566
(Sound of laughter)

1236
00:53:30,933 --> 00:53:32,333
Mash Ghasem!

1237
00:53:32,733 --> 00:53:34,533
Hey, Mash Ghasem!

1238
00:53:35,533 --> 00:53:37,633
Come on, Babajoon wants you!

1239
00:53:41,366 --> 00:53:43,366
What does Mr. Colonel want with us?!

1240
00:53:43,566 --> 00:53:45,766
They wanna ask you somethin’.

1241
00:53:45,800 --> 00:53:47,800
God, let this go well.

1242
00:53:49,366 --> 00:53:51,600
(Sound of whispering)

1243
00:53:52,333 --> 00:53:54,166
- Well, well, Mash Ghasem!

1244
00:53:54,200 --> 00:53:56,266
- Welcome, sit down! - Come in!

1245
00:53:57,033 --> 00:53:57,566
Well…

1246
00:53:58,266 --> 00:53:59,366
Mr. Mash Ghasem!

1247
00:53:59,700 --> 00:54:00,833
Your testimony,

1248
00:54:00,833 --> 00:54:04,633
Is needed for the unity of a noble family!

1249
00:54:05,433 --> 00:54:08,833
Swear to tell nothing but the truth!

1250
00:54:09,300 --> 00:54:11,766
Sir, when have we ever lied!?

1251
00:54:12,033 --> 00:54:13,666
Mr. Mash Ghasem!

1252
00:54:14,000 --> 00:54:14,966
You,

1253
00:54:15,200 --> 00:54:18,700
At Mr. Colonel’s party that night,

1254
00:54:19,066 --> 00:54:23,900
When a sound went off in the middle of Sir’s speech,

1255
00:54:24,066 --> 00:54:26,500
Did you hear the sound with your own ears or not?

1256
00:54:26,500 --> 00:54:27,066
Yes?

1257
00:54:28,300 --> 00:54:29,533
Honestly, Sir, why should I lie!

1258
00:54:29,600 --> 00:54:31,700
The grave is just this far, A-A-A-A!

1259
00:54:32,333 --> 00:54:33,666
Mr. Mash Ghasem!

1260
00:54:33,900 --> 00:54:36,733
You’re standing before a judge!

1261
00:54:37,300 --> 00:54:39,066
What’s this ‘A-A-A-A’?!

1262
00:54:40,366 --> 00:54:41,833
Sorry, Your Highness!

1263
00:54:41,866 --> 00:54:43,666
It’s Mash Ghasem’s habit!

1264
00:54:43,700 --> 00:54:46,100
It means the grave is only four fingers away.

1265
00:54:46,133 --> 00:54:47,466
A-A-A-A!

1266
00:54:47,500 --> 00:54:48,666
Why would I lie!

1267
00:54:48,666 --> 00:54:49,566
(Crowd laughter)

1268
00:54:49,600 --> 00:54:51,966
Mr. Mash Ghasem, please,

1269
00:54:52,466 --> 00:54:53,933
Don’t repeat that gesture.

1270
00:54:54,300 --> 00:54:56,166
Answer my question.

1271
00:54:56,433 --> 00:54:57,233
Yes, sir!

1272
00:54:58,300 --> 00:55:00,633
Yes, Sir! At your service!

1273
00:55:01,100 --> 00:55:03,400
You said that that Suspishes sound…

1274
00:55:03,433 --> 00:55:05,900
Suspicious! Suspicious, sir!

1275
00:55:06,300 --> 00:55:07,100
What does it mean?!

1276
00:55:07,366 --> 00:55:08,600
“What does it mean” means what!?

1277
00:55:08,933 --> 00:55:10,866
You said Suspishes,

1278
00:55:11,366 --> 00:55:13,033
I told you to say Suspicious!

1279
00:55:14,100 --> 00:55:14,966
Honestly, Sir!

1280
00:55:15,566 --> 00:55:16,533
Why lie!

1281
00:55:16,566 --> 00:55:18,133
Now, what’s the difference?

1282
00:55:18,166 --> 00:55:19,766
Difference in what?

1283
00:55:19,966 --> 00:55:23,333
The difference between what we said and what you said!

1284
00:55:23,400 --> 00:55:24,133
Oh my…

1285
00:55:24,166 --> 00:55:26,566
Sir, a suspicious sound means… (Makes a farting sound with his mouth)

1286
00:55:26,566 --> 00:55:28,600
(Crowd laughter)

1287
00:55:28,633 --> 00:55:31,300
Moment, Moment, Moment (Crowd laughter)

1288
00:55:31,333 --> 00:55:32,066
Quiet! (Crowd laughter)

1289
00:55:32,100 --> 00:55:33,233
Come on, sir, it’s not funny! (Crowd laughter)

1290
00:55:33,266 --> 00:55:34,000
Quiet! (Crowd laughter)

1291
00:55:34,033 --> 00:55:35,433
Quiet! - Bless you!

1292
00:55:35,466 --> 00:55:38,800
Sir, you shouldn’t joke with justice and the court!

1293
00:55:38,833 --> 00:55:40,033
Brother, please sit down! (Crowd laughter)

1294
00:55:40,066 --> 00:55:41,233
Why are you getting angry?

1295
00:55:41,233 --> 00:55:42,000
I was explaining!

1296
00:55:42,033 --> 00:55:43,533
I was describing the scene!

1297
00:55:43,566 --> 00:55:44,633
Please, you go ahead and sit down!

1298
00:55:44,666 --> 00:55:47,100
I wanted Mash Ghasem to understand your meaning! (Crowd laughter)

1299
00:55:47,100 --> 00:55:47,800
Quiet!

1300
00:55:47,833 --> 00:55:49,266
Quiet! Moment. What’s that?

1301
00:55:50,166 --> 00:55:50,800
Well!

1302
00:55:50,833 --> 00:55:53,266
Mash Ghasem, now that you understand what’s meant,

1303
00:55:53,700 --> 00:55:56,833
Tell me, this suspicious sound,

1304
00:55:56,833 --> 00:55:58,800
Did you hear it with your own ears or not?

1305
00:55:59,266 --> 00:56:01,833
Honestly, Sir, L… L… L… L

1306
00:56:01,866 --> 00:56:04,466
Do you want the lie or the truth?

1307
00:56:04,866 --> 00:56:06,300
Bless you!

1308
00:56:06,333 --> 00:56:07,966
Bless you!

1309
00:56:08,633 --> 00:56:11,400
What is this, man! Are you joking?!

1310
00:56:11,666 --> 00:56:13,633
When Mr. Shamsali Mirza,

1311
00:56:13,666 --> 00:56:15,566
Asks you a question,

1312
00:56:15,566 --> 00:56:18,500
Well, obviously, he wants the truth!

1313
00:56:19,266 --> 00:56:20,033
Honestly…

1314
00:56:20,600 --> 00:56:23,366
I… I think it was that sound, y… y… yes!

1315
00:56:23,366 --> 00:56:25,000
That very sound, yes!

1316
00:56:25,033 --> 00:56:27,866
(Crowd laughter)

1317
00:56:27,900 --> 00:56:30,666
The answer to the first question has been given.

1318
00:56:31,200 --> 00:56:33,433
Now let’s move on to the second question.

1319
00:56:33,933 --> 00:56:35,600
Mr. Mash Ghasem!

1320
00:56:36,066 --> 00:56:40,133
You who were present at the party that night,

1321
00:56:40,966 --> 00:56:41,966
Tell me,

1322
00:56:42,333 --> 00:56:44,366
That suspicious sound,

1323
00:56:44,966 --> 00:56:47,200
Who did it come from?

1324
00:56:47,400 --> 00:56:47,900
Huh?

1325
00:56:47,933 --> 00:56:48,700
Honestly…

1326
00:56:49,500 --> 00:56:50,900
Honestly…

1327
00:56:51,133 --> 00:56:52,166
Why lie?!

1328
00:56:52,466 --> 00:56:54,666
The grave is this close!

1329
00:56:55,400 --> 00:56:57,566
We were listening to Sir,

1330
00:56:57,600 --> 00:57:00,533
He was telling the story of the Kazerun war.

1331
00:57:01,066 --> 00:57:01,666
He was sayin’:

1332
00:57:01,700 --> 00:57:04,833
He aimed right at Mr. Khodadad Khan’s forehead,

1333
00:57:04,833 --> 00:57:05,866
And pulled the trigger.

1334
00:57:06,466 --> 00:57:07,900
The first shot missed!

1335
00:57:07,966 --> 00:57:10,200
Right by Khodadad Khan’s ear!

1336
00:57:10,233 --> 00:57:10,766
Mash Ghasem!

1337
00:57:10,800 --> 00:57:11,400
Yes… yes… yes!

1338
00:57:11,400 --> 00:57:13,500
Brother didn’t get to that part!

1339
00:57:13,800 --> 00:57:17,066
He only got to aiming at Khodadad Khan’s head!

1340
00:57:17,100 --> 00:57:17,900
Yes, Sir!

1341
00:57:17,933 --> 00:57:19,833
Well, we saw it with our own eyes,

1342
00:57:19,866 --> 00:57:21,766
We’ll tell you the story ourselves! - Mash Ghasem!

1343
00:57:22,666 --> 00:57:24,266
No need to tell it!

1344
00:57:24,400 --> 00:57:27,300
Just answer His Highness’s questions.

1345
00:57:27,433 --> 00:57:28,366
Honestly…

1346
00:57:29,566 --> 00:57:30,400
Honestly…

1347
00:57:30,433 --> 00:57:31,533
Why lie!

1348
00:57:32,333 --> 00:57:35,566
We… when the sound came, our attention was on Sir.

1349
00:57:36,033 --> 00:57:38,066
When we turned around, first there was

1350
00:57:38,400 --> 00:57:40,400
Your sister’s husband,

1351
00:57:41,100 --> 00:57:43,866
And behind him, Miss Ghamar!

1352
00:57:43,966 --> 00:57:44,633
What?!

1353
00:57:44,633 --> 00:57:45,400
Ghamar?!

1354
00:57:45,433 --> 00:57:47,300
Mrs Aziz al-Saltaneh, please!

1355
00:57:47,333 --> 00:57:49,200
Calm down, calm down. - What’s that, listen to what he’s sayin’!

1356
00:57:49,233 --> 00:57:50,700
He’s talkin’! - Quiet!

1357
00:57:52,833 --> 00:57:55,700
Shazdeh, if you agree, I have a proposal.

1358
00:57:55,733 --> 00:57:57,633
Talk about the reservoir. - Alright.

1359
00:57:57,666 --> 00:57:59,733
In my opinion, there’s no problem at all.

1360
00:57:59,933 --> 00:58:01,333
I completely agree.

1361
00:58:02,233 --> 00:58:05,000
No one said anything to upset you, Mrs Aziz!

1362
00:58:05,033 --> 00:58:06,233
What else did you want them to say?

1363
00:58:06,533 --> 00:58:09,033
We recall one day in the Kazerun war,

1364
00:58:09,233 --> 00:58:10,366
One of our men had been shot

1365
00:58:10,400 --> 00:58:12,600
Right between the eyes!

1366
00:58:12,733 --> 00:58:14,200
It went out the back of his head.

1367
00:58:14,833 --> 00:58:16,333
The poor guy was from Malayer.

1368
00:58:16,866 --> 00:58:19,300
No matter how much we tried to put him on the horse’s back,

1369
00:58:19,500 --> 00:58:21,700
To take him out of the battlefield,

1370
00:58:21,733 --> 00:58:23,233
He just wouldn’t agree!

1371
00:58:24,166 --> 00:58:26,166
He said, Mash Ghasem, you go!

1372
00:58:26,666 --> 00:58:28,966
Our time is nearly up.

1373
00:58:29,233 --> 00:58:31,000
But did we leave him? No!

1374
00:58:31,300 --> 00:58:34,166
Mash Ghasem, save these stories for later.

1375
00:58:35,066 --> 00:58:37,933
Are you ready in this critical moment,

1376
00:58:37,966 --> 00:58:39,066
To help us?

1377
00:58:39,100 --> 00:58:39,566
Honestly, Sir…

1378
00:58:39,566 --> 00:58:40,366
Mash Ghasem!

1379
00:58:40,400 --> 00:58:40,966
Yes!

1380
00:58:41,366 --> 00:58:43,133
We’ve almost found a way,

1381
00:58:43,133 --> 00:58:45,833
To resolve the disputes between Brother and Mr. Doctor.

1382
00:58:45,866 --> 00:58:46,633
Yes!

1383
00:58:47,100 --> 00:58:49,066
Only one problem remains.

1384
00:58:50,300 --> 00:58:53,333
That’s the matter of the suspicious sound from the party night.

1385
00:58:54,333 --> 00:58:56,400
Cusre on whoever did it!

1386
00:58:56,466 --> 00:58:57,333
Mash Ghasem?

1387
00:58:57,933 --> 00:58:59,200
Remember you said you wanted,

1388
00:58:59,233 --> 00:59:00,866
To build a reservoir in Ghias Abad,

1389
00:59:00,900 --> 00:59:02,066
And dedicate it to the people?

1390
00:59:02,100 --> 00:59:03,633
Yeah? Do you remember?

1391
00:59:05,666 --> 00:59:06,733
Honestly, why should I lie!

1392
00:59:07,766 --> 00:59:10,000
Ever since we were knee-high,

1393
00:59:10,000 --> 00:59:11,266
We wanted it!

1394
00:59:11,533 --> 00:59:14,266
But God never willed us the money for it.

1395
00:59:15,166 --> 00:59:17,033
These poor Ghias Abad folks,

1396
00:59:17,066 --> 00:59:20,233
To this day, they still drink from the same salty Ditchh.

1397
00:59:21,500 --> 00:59:22,266
Mash Ghasem!

1398
00:59:23,133 --> 00:59:24,700
Now, if we’re willing,

1399
00:59:24,733 --> 00:59:27,433
To cover all the costs of this reservoir,

1400
00:59:28,500 --> 00:59:30,766
Are you ready to help us?

1401
00:59:30,800 --> 00:59:31,333
Huh?!

1402
00:59:32,066 --> 00:59:33,800
Well, that’s not bad!

1403
00:59:33,833 --> 00:59:35,333
No offense, but if you told us

1404
00:59:35,333 --> 00:59:37,100
To go to the ends of the earth,

1405
00:59:37,100 --> 00:59:38,866
We’d go and get it done!

1406
00:59:39,000 --> 00:59:40,533
Good man, Mash Ghasem!

1407
00:59:40,566 --> 00:59:41,400
Bravo!

1408
00:59:41,433 --> 00:59:42,966
- I knew he’d agree! - Bravo!

1409
00:59:42,966 --> 00:59:45,833
Come on, well done, well done, bravo…

1410
00:59:45,833 --> 00:59:48,066
Bless you.

1411
00:59:48,100 --> 00:59:49,033
Mash Ghasem!

1412
00:59:49,033 --> 00:59:51,800
The help we’re asking from you is this,

1413
00:59:51,833 --> 00:59:56,033
That you accept that suspicious sound from the party night,

1414
00:59:56,066 --> 00:59:58,733
That went off in the middle of Sir’s speech,

1415
00:59:59,266 --> 01:00:00,866
came from your quarter!

1416
01:00:00,866 --> 01:00:02,200
You mean it came from our neighborhood?

1417
01:00:02,233 --> 01:00:03,633
No… no!

1418
01:00:03,966 --> 01:00:04,966
You didn’t get it!

1419
01:00:05,000 --> 01:00:08,766
I mean that sound came from you!

1420
01:00:08,800 --> 01:00:10,100
Just by accident!

1421
01:00:11,166 --> 01:00:13,600
I swear by the light of this lamp, it wasn’t me!

1422
01:00:13,633 --> 01:00:14,700
Where, Mash Ghasem?

1423
01:00:14,733 --> 01:00:16,733
I swear on Sir’s bread and salt, it wasn’t us!

1424
01:00:16,766 --> 01:00:18,300
- We know it wasn’t you!

1425
01:00:18,333 --> 01:00:20,366
We love Sir more than the apple of our eye,

1426
01:00:20,400 --> 01:00:22,266
Strike us dead if it was us!

1427
01:00:22,266 --> 01:00:24,633
You mean you think we’re that shameless!?

1428
01:00:24,666 --> 01:00:26,266
Mash Ghasem! - Oh man, who said you’re shameless?

1429
01:00:26,900 --> 01:00:29,833
Mash Ghasem! … Why don’t you get it! - Who said you have no shame!

1430
01:00:30,200 --> 01:00:32,933
We all know it wasn’t you! - Yes!

1431
01:00:32,966 --> 01:00:35,200
But we’re askin’ you to make a sacrifice,

1432
01:00:35,233 --> 01:00:36,566
Say it was you.

1433
01:00:36,600 --> 01:00:38,533
So maybe this fight and feud can end!

1434
01:00:38,833 --> 01:00:40,633
You mean we should come and lie?!

1435
01:00:41,366 --> 01:00:43,300
Lie, and to Sir of all people?!

1436
01:00:43,333 --> 01:00:44,466
God forgive me!

1437
01:00:44,500 --> 01:00:46,066
How far is it to the grave?!

1438
01:00:46,600 --> 01:00:48,766
- Hold on… hold on, Mash Ghasem!

1439
01:00:48,766 --> 01:00:50,833
Think about the reservoir!

1440
01:00:50,866 --> 01:00:53,600
They’ll name it the Mash Ghasem Reservoir!

1441
01:00:53,633 --> 01:00:56,200
The blessings of the people of Ghias Abad!

1442
01:00:56,233 --> 01:00:57,066
We should

1443
01:00:57,100 --> 01:00:58,600
Pin shameful stuff like that on ourselves

1444
01:00:58,633 --> 01:01:00,100
So the folks of Ghias Abad can drink water?!

1445
01:01:00,133 --> 01:01:01,933
They can go without for seventy years!

1446
01:01:01,966 --> 01:01:05,466
Oh man, where you goin’ now, Mash Ghasem? (Crowd murmurs)

1447
01:01:05,800 --> 01:01:07,666
If the folks of Ghias Abad find out,

1448
01:01:07,700 --> 01:01:09,866
We built a reservoir with shameful money,

1449
01:01:09,900 --> 01:01:11,966
Even if their water gets saltier,

1450
01:01:11,966 --> 01:01:14,200
They won’t touch a drop for seventy years!

1451
01:01:14,633 --> 01:01:15,366
You think,

1452
01:01:15,400 --> 01:01:17,100
We don’t care about our honor?!

1453
01:01:17,133 --> 01:01:19,300
Do you think we found our honor lying by the road?

1454
01:01:19,333 --> 01:01:20,466
Are you done or not!

1455
01:01:20,800 --> 01:01:21,633
Enough nonsense!

1456
01:01:21,666 --> 01:01:23,133
Enough rubbish!

1457
01:01:23,166 --> 01:01:25,400
Then don’t agree, for all I care!

1458
01:01:25,433 --> 01:01:26,566
Get lost! Get out!

1459
01:01:26,566 --> 01:01:27,333
- Don’t get worked up!

1460
01:01:27,366 --> 01:01:28,700
You shameless fool! - Colonel, don’t upset yourself!

1461
01:01:28,733 --> 01:01:30,533
Go, get lost! - Poor guy doesn’t get it!

1462
01:01:30,533 --> 01:01:31,600
Ugh… what’s that!

1463
01:01:32,000 --> 01:01:34,000
Bless you!

1464
01:01:34,033 --> 01:01:35,233
Ungrateful wretch!

1465
01:01:35,266 --> 01:01:36,900
Bless you!

1466
01:01:37,233 --> 01:01:39,266
Bless you! (He sighs)

1467
01:01:40,133 --> 01:01:42,066
My, my, my… the airs he puts on!

1468
01:01:44,600 --> 01:01:46,666
I suggest we get back to the topic.

1469
01:01:46,933 --> 01:01:48,566
How about continuing the investigation,

1470
01:01:48,600 --> 01:01:50,800
so that the main cause of the sound might be discovered!

1471
01:01:51,933 --> 01:01:52,666
Gentlemen!

1472
01:01:53,266 --> 01:01:54,900
I just had an idea.

1473
01:01:55,933 --> 01:01:58,400
If Mrs Aziz al-Saltaneh agrees,

1474
01:01:58,833 --> 01:02:01,533
I mean, if Mrs Aziz al-Saltaneh, for the sake of

1475
01:02:01,866 --> 01:02:04,233
preserving family unity,

1476
01:02:04,266 --> 01:02:06,366
makes a small sacrifice…

1477
01:02:06,400 --> 01:02:07,166
What kind of sacrifice?!

1478
01:02:09,000 --> 01:02:10,266
If you agree,

1479
01:02:10,266 --> 01:02:12,633
we’ll tell Brother that this thing…

1480
01:02:13,000 --> 01:02:14,700
this little sound,

1481
01:02:14,733 --> 01:02:16,866
came from Miss Ghamar…

1482
01:02:16,866 --> 01:02:17,600
I don’t understand!

1483
01:02:17,633 --> 01:02:18,533
Ghamar what?!

1484
01:02:19,066 --> 01:02:20,266
I said…

1485
01:02:21,133 --> 01:02:22,700
If we tell Brother,

1486
01:02:22,733 --> 01:02:24,066
that that night Ghamar

1487
01:02:24,100 --> 01:02:26,300
was a little unwell…

1488
01:02:26,333 --> 01:02:27,000
What do you mean?

1489
01:02:27,033 --> 01:02:27,833
-It doesn’t get any better than this!

1490
01:02:27,833 --> 01:02:29,066
Have you no shame!

1491
01:02:29,100 --> 01:02:30,800
Aren’t you ashamed, in front of me?!

1492
01:02:31,300 --> 01:02:33,000
Now you’ve gone too far!

1493
01:02:33,333 --> 01:02:34,400
My daughter?!

1494
01:02:34,600 --> 01:02:36,200
My daughter would do such things?!

1495
01:02:36,600 --> 01:02:38,966
I raised her like a little flower!

1496
01:02:39,166 --> 01:02:40,966
Now that a suitor has come for her,

1497
01:02:41,000 --> 01:02:42,966
Now that she’s about to settle down,

1498
01:02:43,000 --> 01:02:44,700
Her relatives are plotting behind her back!

1499
01:02:44,833 --> 01:02:45,733
You people

1500
01:02:45,766 --> 01:02:47,833
can’t stand to see anyone else happy.

1501
01:02:48,133 --> 01:02:50,433
Her first husband left because of you all!

1502
01:02:50,566 --> 01:02:52,533
Now that a suitor has come for her again,

1503
01:02:52,566 --> 01:02:54,300
you want to ruin her reputation and honor!

1504
01:02:54,333 --> 01:02:55,833
Damn you all to hell!

1505
01:02:56,000 --> 01:02:58,033
To hell with your family unity!

1506
01:02:58,066 --> 01:02:59,500
You are right, Mrs Aziz!

1507
01:02:59,500 --> 01:03:00,166
These people,

1508
01:03:00,200 --> 01:03:03,000
don’t consider the reputation and honor of a girl at all!

1509
01:03:03,033 --> 01:03:05,533
Well said, Miss Farokh-Lagha!

1510
01:03:05,833 --> 01:03:06,733
They don’t know that,

1511
01:03:06,733 --> 01:03:09,533
what a struggle it is to raise a daughter and marry her off!

1512
01:03:09,533 --> 01:03:11,500
Everything I suffer is because of them!

1513
01:03:11,533 --> 01:03:13,333
This Mr. Dr. Naser al-Hokama,

1514
01:03:13,500 --> 01:03:14,700
Has spread it around everywhere that…

1515
01:03:14,733 --> 01:03:16,133
Ghamar has no sense! -What happened?

1516
01:03:16,133 --> 01:03:18,433
These very people caused her to divorce her husband!

1517
01:03:18,600 --> 01:03:20,533
They bewitched the poor man!

1518
01:03:20,566 --> 01:03:21,533
They put a lock on his manhood!

1519
01:03:21,566 --> 01:03:22,066
-You’re right!

1520
01:03:22,066 --> 01:03:23,433
My poor daughter,

1521
01:03:23,466 --> 01:03:25,166
She waited for a whole year!

1522
01:03:25,200 --> 01:03:27,900
For a whole year her husband was dying for her!

1523
01:03:27,933 --> 01:03:29,466
But well, what can be done?

1524
01:03:29,466 --> 01:03:30,900
When a man is locked,

1525
01:03:30,933 --> 01:03:32,700
what on earth can the poor guy do?

1526
01:03:32,733 --> 01:03:33,566
Moment!

1527
01:03:33,600 --> 01:03:34,500
Moment!

1528
01:03:34,533 --> 01:03:36,733
It wasn’t her relatives’ fault either!

1529
01:03:36,766 --> 01:03:38,100
So now you’re taking their side too?

1530
01:03:38,133 --> 01:03:39,766
You told us too late!

1531
01:03:39,766 --> 01:03:41,133
If you'd told us earlier,

1532
01:03:41,133 --> 01:03:42,266
we would have done something about it!

1533
01:03:42,633 --> 01:03:43,933
After all, in the family,

1534
01:03:43,966 --> 01:03:45,633
there's always a set of keys that,

1535
01:03:45,666 --> 01:03:47,000
can open the locks!

1536
01:03:47,033 --> 01:03:47,633
-Bravo!

1537
01:03:47,666 --> 01:03:49,333
And we, as relatives,

1538
01:03:49,533 --> 01:03:51,400
are ready to make any sacrifice.

1539
01:03:51,400 --> 01:03:52,866
Damn your ugly face!

1540
01:03:52,900 --> 01:03:55,066
Aren’t you ashamed to say this in front of me? -What do you mean? What do you mean?

1541
01:03:55,100 --> 01:03:56,433
Leave me alone, sir! Leave me alone! -Don’t get angry!

1542
01:03:56,433 --> 01:03:57,133
Why is he doing this?

1543
01:03:57,166 --> 01:03:58,533
Damn you… -Bless you!

1544
01:03:58,566 --> 01:03:59,266
Be ashamed!

1545
01:03:59,300 --> 01:04:00,633
Shame on the lot of you!

1546
01:04:00,666 --> 01:04:01,866
I’m making a suggestion!

1547
01:04:01,866 --> 01:04:03,100
Ghamar! Ghamar!

1548
01:04:03,100 --> 01:04:04,400
Let’s go! -I’m making a sacrifice!

1549
01:04:04,533 --> 01:04:06,200
Have some shame and decency! -Please, don’t get angry!

1550
01:04:06,233 --> 01:04:07,566
-Mrs Aziz, please wait! -What do you mean!

1551
01:04:07,600 --> 01:04:08,766
-They don’t feel shame even in front of me! -Aziz…!

1552
01:04:11,500 --> 01:04:13,966
Really, you’ve overdone it, Shazdeh! -Moment!

1553
01:04:14,333 --> 01:04:16,600
Why are you all giving me dirty looks?

1554
01:04:16,933 --> 01:04:18,433
I said it out of goodwill!

1555
01:04:18,466 --> 01:04:21,466
If my new suitor, God forbid, gets locked,

1556
01:04:21,566 --> 01:04:24,400
everyone should know that as relatives,

1557
01:04:24,400 --> 01:04:25,800
we’re ready for any service!

1558
01:04:26,133 --> 01:04:27,666
I didn’t say anything!

1559
01:04:27,700 --> 01:04:29,733
Aziz jumped down everyone’s throat!

1560
01:04:29,866 --> 01:04:31,066
Didn’t you see what she said to the Doctor?

1561
01:04:31,200 --> 01:04:32,500
What did I say to him?

1562
01:04:32,533 --> 01:04:33,466
Bless you!

1563
01:04:33,500 --> 01:04:34,400
Did I say something wrong?

1564
01:04:34,800 --> 01:04:36,400
If I said something wrong, say it!

1565
01:04:36,800 --> 01:04:38,466
You can’t even say anything!

1566
01:04:43,200 --> 01:04:44,100
Dad!

1567
01:04:44,366 --> 01:04:45,100
What are you saying?

1568
01:04:47,333 --> 01:04:49,400
What does “locked” mean?

1569
01:04:50,433 --> 01:04:52,133
At your age,

1570
01:04:52,366 --> 01:04:54,333
you don’t know what “locked” means?

1571
01:04:54,333 --> 01:04:55,233
Then what do you know?

1572
01:04:55,433 --> 01:04:56,900
How should I know?

1573
01:04:57,133 --> 01:04:59,166
It means no San Francisco!

1574
01:04:59,166 --> 01:05:01,066
Ah… Asdollah!

1575
01:05:01,100 --> 01:05:03,166
When is this the time for jokes? -What? I’m just saying the meaning!

1576
01:05:03,200 --> 01:05:06,000
It seems this has become a joke!

1577
01:05:06,033 --> 01:05:08,266
In that case, with your permission… !Moment…Moment

1578
01:05:08,266 --> 01:05:10,366
Please don’t get angry, brother!

1579
01:05:10,400 --> 01:05:12,500
I’m seriously trying to find a solution!

1580
01:05:12,933 --> 01:05:14,800
I want to ask Colonel,

1581
01:05:14,800 --> 01:05:16,333
why exactly,

1582
01:05:16,366 --> 01:05:18,133
do we need Mrs. Aziz al-Saltaneh’s consent?

1583
01:05:18,133 --> 01:05:18,833
Huh?

1584
01:05:19,066 --> 01:05:21,600
Why is it necessary to put her in the loop? -Ah…

1585
01:05:22,600 --> 01:05:23,733
Actually, Colonel,

1586
01:05:23,766 --> 01:05:25,533
you yourself go and tell him

1587
01:05:25,700 --> 01:05:27,333
that this act was Ghamar’s!

1588
01:05:27,366 --> 01:05:29,500
Yes, really, what’s the need

1589
01:05:29,900 --> 01:05:31,966
to tell Mrs. Aziz al-Saltaneh about it?

1590
01:05:32,000 --> 01:05:32,533
Exactly!

1591
01:05:33,300 --> 01:05:34,100
I’ve tried so much,

1592
01:05:34,133 --> 01:05:36,466
to reconcile my brother-in-law and Brother,

1593
01:05:36,500 --> 01:05:37,566
that

1594
01:05:37,600 --> 01:05:39,233
he no longer believes me.

1595
01:05:39,266 --> 01:05:40,866
There’s no point in my going.

1596
01:05:40,900 --> 01:05:42,233
Moment!

1597
01:05:42,700 --> 01:05:45,233
How about we ask Dr. Naser al-Hokama

1598
01:05:45,266 --> 01:05:47,066
to do this job for us!

1599
01:05:47,300 --> 01:05:48,733
Bless you!

1600
01:05:48,766 --> 01:05:50,266
Bless you!

1601
01:05:50,366 --> 01:05:52,133
Yes, sir!

1602
01:05:52,133 --> 01:05:52,866
Exactly!

1603
01:05:52,900 --> 01:05:56,033
Actually, I’ve repeatedly,

1604
01:05:56,233 --> 01:05:59,433
told Mrs. Aziz al-Saltaneh

1605
01:05:59,466 --> 01:06:02,200
that Miss Ghamar,

1606
01:06:02,233 --> 01:06:04,600
needs treatment! -Exactly!

1607
01:06:04,833 --> 01:06:06,466
This girl’s fat!

1608
01:06:06,500 --> 01:06:06,933
Yeah!

1609
01:06:06,933 --> 01:06:08,866
She eats too much. -Yeah, true!

1610
01:06:08,866 --> 01:06:11,766
She eats gassy stuff!

1611
01:06:11,800 --> 01:06:12,633
Exactly!

1612
01:06:12,666 --> 01:06:14,733
Bravo... bravo... exactly!

1613
01:06:14,766 --> 01:06:17,800
Well, she doesn’t have much sense either!

1614
01:06:17,800 --> 01:06:19,200
Naturally!

1615
01:06:19,233 --> 01:06:20,700
Gentlemen!

1616
01:06:20,733 --> 01:06:21,766
When—

1617
01:06:21,800 --> 01:06:22,766
the mind

1618
01:06:22,800 --> 01:06:24,133
is missing,

1619
01:06:24,300 --> 01:06:26,566
and the stomach’s full of gas,

1620
01:06:26,633 --> 01:06:29,633
these sounds are inevitable!

1621
01:06:29,966 --> 01:06:31,666
Gentlemen!

1622
01:06:32,466 --> 01:06:34,100
I shall go myself!

1623
01:06:34,700 --> 01:06:37,766
-Bravo... that’s right... good... yes, exactly...

1624
01:06:38,766 --> 01:06:42,000
I even swear on the soul of the late Great Sir,

1625
01:06:42,033 --> 01:06:43,633
that I myself heard it

1626
01:06:43,666 --> 01:06:46,100
with my own ears that night,

1627
01:06:46,500 --> 01:06:48,866
and I even pinpointed where it came from!

1628
01:06:49,066 --> 01:06:51,533
Yes, sir!

1629
01:06:51,666 --> 01:06:52,800
Bless you!

1630
01:06:52,833 --> 01:06:54,000
-The doctor is leaving.

1631
01:06:54,000 --> 01:06:55,033
Bless you!

1632
01:06:55,066 --> 01:06:56,400
-I doubt it.

1633
01:06:56,433 --> 01:06:57,800
-I don’t think he’ll agree!

1634
01:07:15,300 --> 01:07:16,266
Hello, Doctor!

1635
01:07:16,266 --> 01:07:18,000
Hello, my boy, how are you?

1636
01:07:18,033 --> 01:07:19,700
Bless you!

1637
01:07:42,733 --> 01:07:44,900
Hello, Doctor! - Hello!

1638
01:07:44,933 --> 01:07:46,766
Where is Sir right now?

1639
01:07:46,800 --> 01:07:49,266
First, Sir was in this room,

1640
01:07:49,300 --> 01:07:51,333
then, via the corridor, he went to that room.

1641
01:07:51,333 --> 01:07:52,366
So now he’s there!

1642
01:07:52,366 --> 01:07:53,200
Right there!

1643
01:07:53,200 --> 01:07:53,666
Yes!

1644
01:07:53,666 --> 01:07:54,766
Bless you!

1645
01:07:54,800 --> 01:07:55,733
If you see him,

1646
01:07:55,766 --> 01:07:57,533
don’t say we told you where he is!

1647
01:07:57,566 --> 01:08:00,366
If Sir finds out, he’ll chop us to bits! - Bless you!

1648
01:08:26,566 --> 01:08:28,100
By the way...

1649
01:08:43,333 --> 01:08:44,600
Bro!

1650
01:08:44,900 --> 01:08:46,000
Do you have a match?

1651
01:08:46,033 --> 01:08:47,300
- No! - You don't have one...

1652
01:08:52,100 --> 01:08:53,466
Ma...match?

1653
01:08:53,500 --> 01:08:54,866
No...I don't. No!

1654
01:09:00,900 --> 01:09:01,800
Match?

1655
01:09:01,833 --> 01:09:02,500
No...no!

1656
01:09:07,766 --> 01:09:08,566
Match?

1657
01:09:08,600 --> 01:09:10,400
Cigarettes aren't good for your heart.

1658
01:09:22,200 --> 01:09:23,800
- Hope everything's fine!

1659
01:09:35,600 --> 01:09:37,066
Gentlemen!

1660
01:09:37,100 --> 01:09:38,933
Bless you!

1661
01:09:39,200 --> 01:09:40,333
What happened, Doctor?!

1662
01:09:40,333 --> 01:09:41,433
What happened? Huh?

1663
01:09:41,866 --> 01:09:44,300
Sir is very regretful that,

1664
01:09:44,333 --> 01:09:46,866
he rushed to judgment!

1665
01:09:48,233 --> 01:09:50,833
They promised to go tomorrow,

1666
01:09:50,866 --> 01:09:53,366
and apologize to their sister's husband!

1667
01:09:53,400 --> 01:09:54,800
Moment! Moment! (laughter)

1668
01:09:54,833 --> 01:09:56,433
Since I’m a member of the Foreign Ministry,

1669
01:09:56,466 --> 01:09:57,533
I suggest Dr. Naser Al-Hokama

1670
01:09:57,566 --> 01:09:59,633
for the presidency of the United Nations!

1671
01:09:59,666 --> 01:10:01,966
(laughter)

1672
01:10:03,500 --> 01:10:04,366
Moment!

1673
01:10:05,000 --> 01:10:06,933
The family unity has been saved!

1674
01:10:06,966 --> 01:10:07,733
But be careful,

1675
01:10:07,766 --> 01:10:09,333
don’t let Ghamar’s suitor hear anything!

1676
01:10:09,366 --> 01:10:10,366
Otherwise, Mrs. Aziz Al-saltaneh,

1677
01:10:10,400 --> 01:10:12,800
will lock up the whole lot of us!

1678
01:10:12,933 --> 01:10:14,733
(laughter)

1679
01:10:15,700 --> 01:10:18,200
Excuse me! Excuse me! Excuse me!

1680
01:10:18,200 --> 01:10:20,033
I suggest we all go together,

1681
01:10:20,066 --> 01:10:22,333
to pay a visit to my dear sister’s husband.

1682
01:10:22,366 --> 01:10:25,700
(murmur and laughter)

1683
01:10:25,700 --> 01:10:26,600
All together!

1684
01:10:26,633 --> 01:10:28,533
-Bless you! (murmur and laughter)

1685
01:10:28,566 --> 01:10:29,500
Go ahead!

1686
01:10:29,500 --> 01:10:32,066
(murmur and laughter)

1687
01:10:32,100 --> 01:10:32,933
Shajoon!

1688
01:10:33,233 --> 01:10:34,266
Shajoon!

1689
01:10:34,466 --> 01:10:35,600
What is it? I'm here!

1690
01:10:36,933 --> 01:10:38,066
Uncle has promised to come,

1691
01:10:38,066 --> 01:10:39,633
to apologize to Agha Joon!

1692
01:10:39,633 --> 01:10:40,633
In fact, my foolishness

1693
01:10:40,666 --> 01:10:42,233
is a blessing for some people! - Now that he’s backed down,

1694
01:10:42,266 --> 01:10:43,600
- you back down too!

1695
01:10:43,800 --> 01:10:45,200
I’m begging you, dear!

1696
01:10:45,233 --> 01:10:46,366
For the sake of your departed loved ones,

1697
01:10:46,400 --> 01:10:48,300
don't pursue it anymore! - Okay, I won't pursue it!

1698
01:10:49,366 --> 01:10:52,133
I'll show him a Kazerun war he'll never forget!

1699
01:10:53,966 --> 01:10:57,600
♪ Ride of the valkyrie ♪

